<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<usx version="2.6">
  <book code="JDG" style="id">- Tov Rose New Messianic Version Bible</book>
  <para style="h">Judges</para>
  <para style="mt">Judges</para>
  <chapter number="1" style="c" />
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="1" style="v" />Now after the death of Y’hoshua <char style="add">[Yehovah is Salvation]</char> it came to pass, that the people of Yisra’el <char style="add">[He Holds Onto The Heel Of God]</char> asked the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char>, saying, Who shall go up for us against the Kena’ani <char style="add">[Merchant]</char> first, to fight against them?</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="2" style="v" />And the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> said, Y’hudah <char style="add">[Let Him (God) Be Praised]</char> shall go up: behold, I have delivered the land into his hand.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="3" style="v" />And Y’hudah <char style="add">[Let Him (God) Be Praised]</char> said unto Shim’on <char style="add">[he who hears]</char> his brother, Come up with me into my lot, that we may fight against the Kena’ani <char style="add">[Merchant]</char>; and I likewise will go with you<char style="ord">i</char> into you<char style="ord">i</char> lot. So Shim’on <char style="add">[he who hears]</char> went with him.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="4" style="v" />And Y’hudah <char style="add">[Let Him (God) Be Praised]</char> went up; and the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> delivered the Kena’ani <char style="add">[Merchant]</char> and the P’rizi <char style="add">[Dwellers in Unwalled Towns]</char> into their hand: and they killed of them in Bezek <char style="add">[Lightning]</char> ten thousand men.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="5" style="v" />And they found Adonis--Bezek <char style="add">[My Lord is Lightning]</char> in Bezek <char style="add">[Lightning]</char>: and they fought against him, and they killed the Kena’ani <char style="add">[Merchant]</char> and the P’rizi <char style="add">[Dwellers in Unwalled Towns]</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="6" style="v" />But Adonis--Bezek <char style="add">[My Lord is Lightning]</char> fled; and they pursued after him, and caught him, and cut off his thumbs and his great toes.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="7" style="v" />And Adonis--Bezek <char style="add">[My Lord is Lightning]</char> said, Threescore and ten kings, having their thumbs and their great toes cut off, gathered <char style="add">[their meat]</char> under my table: as I have done, so God-Elōhīm <char style="pn">(The Living Word)</char> <char style="add">[The Many Powered]</char> has requited me. And they brought him to Yerushalayim <char style="add">[Foundation of Peace]</char>, and there he died.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="8" style="v" />Now the children of Y’hudah <char style="add">[Let Him (God) Be Praised]</char> had fought against Yerushalayim <char style="add">[Foundation of Peace]</char>, and had taken it, and smitten it with the edge of the sword, and set the city on fire.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="9" style="v" />And afterward the children of Y’hudah <char style="add">[Let Him (God) Be Praised]</char> went down to fight against the Kena’ani <char style="add">[Merchant]</char>, that dwelt in the mountain, and in the south, and in the valley.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="10" style="v" />And Y’hudah <char style="add">[Let Him (God) Be Praised]</char> went against the Kena’ani <char style="add">[Merchant]</char> that dwelt in Hevron <char style="add">[Seat of Association]</char>: (now the name of Hevron <char style="add">[Seat of Association]</char> before <char style="add">[was]</char> Kiryat-Arba <char style="add">[City of Arba (four)]</char>:) and they killed Sheshai <char style="add">[Noble]</char>, and Achiman <char style="add">[My Brother is a Gift]</char>, and Talmai <char style="add">[Plowman]</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="11" style="v" />And from there he went against the inhabitants of D’vir <char style="add">[Sanctuary]</char>: and the name of D’vir <char style="add">[Sanctuary]</char> before <char style="add">[was]</char> Kiryat-Sepher <char style="add">[City of the Book]</char>:</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="12" style="v" />And Kalev <char style="add">[Dog]</char> said, He that smites Kiryat-Sepher <char style="add">[City of the Book]</char>, and takes it, to him will I give ‘Akhsah <char style="add">[Anklet]</char> my daughter to wife.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="13" style="v" />And ‘Otni’el <char style="add">[Lion of God]</char> the son of K’naz <char style="add">[Hunter]</char>, Kalev <char style="add">[Dog]</char>’s younger brother, took it: and he gave him ‘Akhsah <char style="add">[Anklet]</char> his daughter to wife.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="14" style="v" />And it came to pass, when she came <char style="add">[to him]</char>, that she moved him to ask of her father a field: and she lighted from off <char style="add">[her]</char> ass; and Kalev <char style="add">[Dog]</char> said unto her, What will you<char style="ord">i</char>?</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="15" style="v" />And she said unto him, Give me a blessing: for you<char style="ord">i</char> have given me a south land; give me also springs of water. And Kalev <char style="add">[Dog]</char> gave her the upper springs and the lower springs.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="16" style="v" />And the children of the Kayin <char style="add">[Possession]</char>, Moshe <char style="add">[He Who Draws Out Of The Waters]</char>’ father in law, went up out of the city of palm trees with the children of Y’hudah <char style="add">[Let Him (God) Be Praised]</char> into the wilderness of Y’hudah <char style="add">[Let Him (God) Be Praised]</char>, which <char style="add">[lies]</char> in the south of ‘Arad <char style="add">[A Wild Ass]</char>; and they went and dwelt among the people.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="17" style="v" />And Y’hudah <char style="add">[Let Him (God) Be Praised]</char> went with Shim’on <char style="add">[he who hears]</char> his brother, and they killed the Kena’ani <char style="add">[Merchant]</char> that inhabited Zephath, and utterly destroyed it. And the name of the city was called Hormah <char style="add">[Asylum]</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="18" style="v" />Also Y’hudah <char style="add">[Let Him (God) Be Praised]</char> took ‘Azah <char style="add">[The Strong]</char> with the coast thereof, and Askelon <char style="add">[The Fire of Infamy: I shall be Weighed]</char> with the coast thereof, and ‘Ekron <char style="add">[Torn Up by the Roots]</char> with the coast thereof.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="19" style="v" />And the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> was with Y’hudah <char style="add">[Let Him (God) Be Praised]</char>; and he drove out <char style="add">[the inhabitants of]</char> the mountain; but could not drive out the inhabitants of the valley, because they had chariots of iron.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="20" style="v" />And they gave Hevron <char style="add">[Seat of Association]</char> unto Kalev <char style="add">[Dog]</char>, as Moshe <char style="add">[He Who Draws Out Of The Waters]</char> said: and he expelled there the three sons of Anak <char style="add">[Neck]</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="21" style="v" />And the children of Binyamin <char style="add">[Son of the Right Hand/Strength]</char> did not drive out the Y’vusi <char style="add">[Threshers, Trampled Under Foot]</char> that inhabited Yerushalayim <char style="add">[Foundation of Peace]</char>; but the Y’vusi <char style="add">[Threshers, Trampled Under Foot]</char> dwell with the children of Binyamin <char style="add">[Son of the Right Hand/Strength]</char> in Yerushalayim <char style="add">[Foundation of Peace]</char> unto this day.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="22" style="v" />And the house of Yosef <char style="add">[(God) He Shall Add]</char>, they also went up against Beit-El <char style="add">[House of God]</char>: and the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> <char style="add">[was]</char> with them.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="23" style="v" />And the house of Yosef [<char style="pn">(God)</char> He Shall Add] sent to descry <char style="pn">(search out; map out; to describe)</char> Beit-El <char style="add">[House of God]</char>. (Now the name of the city before <char style="add">[was]</char> Luz <char style="add">[Almond Tree]</char>.)</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="24" style="v" />And the spies saw a man come forth out of the city, and they said unto him, Show us, we pray you<char style="ord">i</char>, the entrance into the city, and we will show you<char style="ord">i</char> mercy.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="25" style="v" />And when he showed them the entrance into the city, they struck the city with the edge of the sword; but they let go the man and all his family.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="26" style="v" />And the man went into the land of the Hitti <char style="add">[Terrorists]</char>, and built a city, and called the name thereof Luz <char style="add">[Almond Tree]</char>: which <char style="add">[is]</char> the name thereof unto this day.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="27" style="v" />Neither did M’nasheh <char style="add">[Causing to Forget]</char> drive out <char style="add">[the inhabitants of]</char> Beit-Sh’an <char style="add">[House of Ease]</char> and her towns, nor Ta’anakh <char style="add">[Sandy]</char> and her towns, nor the inhabitants of Dor <char style="add">[Generation]</char> and her towns, nor the inhabitants of Yivle’am <char style="add">[Devouring the People]</char> and her towns, nor the inhabitants of Megiddo <char style="add">[Place of Crowds]</char> and her towns: but the Kena’ani <char style="add">[Merchant]</char> would dwell in that land.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="28" style="v" />And it came to pass, when Yisra’el <char style="add">[He Holds Onto The Heel Of God]</char> was strong, that they put the Kena’ani <char style="add">[Merchant]</char> to tribute, and did not utterly drive them out.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="29" style="v" />Neither did Efrayim <char style="add">[Doubly Fruitful]</char> drive out the Kena’ani <char style="add">[Merchant]</char> that dwelt in Gezer <char style="add">[Portion]</char>; but the Kena’ani <char style="add">[Merchant]</char> dwelt in Gezer <char style="add">[Portion]</char> among them.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="30" style="v" />Neither did Z’vulun <char style="add">[Glorious Dwelling Place]</char> drive out the inhabitants of Kitron <char style="add">[Incense]</char>, nor the inhabitants of Nahalol <char style="add">[Pasture]</char>; but the Kena’ani <char style="add">[Merchant]</char> dwelt among them, and became tributaries.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="31" style="v" />Neither did Asher <char style="add">[Happy]</char> drive out the inhabitants of ‘Akko <char style="add">[His Straitness]</char>, nor the inhabitants of Tzidon <char style="add">[Hunting]</char>, nor of Ahlav <char style="add">[Fertile Place]</char>, nor of Achziv <char style="add">[Deceit]</char>, nor of Helbah <char style="add">[Fertile]</char>, nor of Afik <char style="add">[Enclosure]</char>, nor of Rechov <char style="add">[Broad Place]</char>:</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="32" style="v" />But the Asheri <char style="add">[Happy]</char> dwelt among the Kena’ani <char style="add">[Merchant]</char>, the inhabitants of the land: for they did not drive them out.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="33" style="v" />Neither did Naftali <char style="add">[My Wrestling]</char> drive out the inhabitants of Beit-Shemesh <char style="add">[House of the Sun]</char>, nor the inhabitants of Beit-’Anat <char style="add">[House of Response (or Affliction)]</char>; but he dwelt among the Kena’ani <char style="add">[Merchant]</char>, the inhabitants of the land: nevertheless the inhabitants of Beit-Shemesh <char style="add">[House of the Sun]</char> and of Beit-’Anat <char style="add">[House of Response (or Affliction)]</char> became tributaries unto them.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="34" style="v" />And the Emori <char style="add">[Highlanders]</char> forced the children of Dan <char style="add">[Judge]</char> into the mountain: for they would not suffer them to come down to the valley:</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="35" style="v" />But the Emori <char style="add">[Highlanders]</char> would dwell in mount Heres <char style="add">[The Sun]</char> in Ayalon <char style="add">[Field of Deer]</char>, and in Sha’alvim <char style="add">[Place of Foxes]</char>: yet the hand of the house of Yosef [<char style="pn">(God)</char> He Shall Add] prevailed, so that they became tributaries.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="36" style="v" />And the coast of the Emori <char style="add">[Highlanders] [was]</char> from the going up to ‘Akrabbim <char style="add">[Ascent of Scorpions]</char>, from the rock, and upward.</para>
  <chapter number="2" style="c" />
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="1" style="v" />And an angel of the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> came up from Gilgal <char style="add">[A Wheel, Rolling]</char> to Bokhim <char style="add">[Weeping]</char>, and said, I made you to go up out of Mitzrayim <char style="add">[Egypt - The Narrow Place]</char>, and have brought you unto the land which I swore unto your fathers; and I said, I will never break my covenant with you.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="2" style="v" />And you<char style="ord">2f</char> shall make no league with the inhabitants of this land; you<char style="ord">2f</char> shall throw down their altars: but you<char style="ord">2f</char> have not obeyed my voice: why have you<char style="ord">2f</char> done this?</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="3" style="v" />For what reason I also said, I will not drive them out from before you; but they shall be <char style="add">[as thorns]</char> in your sides, and their gods shall be a snare unto you.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="4" style="v" />And it came to pass, when the angel of the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> spoke these words unto all the people of Yisra’el <char style="add">[He Holds Onto The Heel Of God]</char>, that the people lifted up their voice, and wept.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="5" style="v" />And they called the name of that place Bokhim <char style="add">[Weeping]</char>: and they sacrificed there unto the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="6" style="v" />And when Y’hoshua <char style="add">[Yehovah is Salvation]</char> had let the people go, the people of Yisra’el <char style="add">[He Holds Onto The Heel Of God]</char> went every man unto his inheritance to possess the land.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="7" style="v" />And the people served the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> all the days of Y’hoshua <char style="add">[Yehovah is Salvation]</char>, and all the days of the elders that outlived Y’hoshua <char style="add">[Yehovah is Salvation]</char>, who had seen all the great works of the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char>, that he did for Yisra’el <char style="add">[He Holds Onto The Heel Of God]</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="8" style="v" />And Y’hoshua <char style="add">[Yehovah is Salvation]</char> the son of Nun <char style="add">[Posterity]</char>, the servant of the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char>, died, <char style="add">[being]</char> an hundred and ten years old.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="9" style="v" />And they buried him in the border of his inheritance in Timnat-Heres <char style="add">[Portion of the Sun]</char>, in the mount of Efrayim <char style="add">[Doubly Fruitful]</char>, on the north side of the hill Ga’ash <char style="add">[Quaking]</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="10" style="v" />And also all that generation were gathered unto their fathers: and there arose another generation after them, which knew not the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char>, nor yet the works which he had done for Yisra’el <char style="add">[He Holds Onto The Heel Of God]</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="11" style="v" />And the people of Yisra’el <char style="add">[He Holds Onto The Heel Of God]</char> did evil in the sight of the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char>, and served Ba’alim <char style="add">[lords (false gods)]</char>:</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="12" style="v" />And they forsook the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> God-Elōhīm <char style="pn">(The Living Word)</char> <char style="add">[The Many Powered]</char> of their fathers, which brought them out of the land of Mitzrayim <char style="add">[Egypt - The Narrow Place]</char>, and followed other gods, of the gods of the people that <char style="add">[were]</char> round about them, and bowed themselves unto them, and provoked the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> to anger.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="13" style="v" />And they forsook the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char>, and served Ba’al <char style="add">[lord (a false god)]</char> and ‘Ashtarot <char style="add">[Star (female deity)]</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="14" style="v" />And the anger of the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> was hot against Yisra’el <char style="add">[He Holds Onto The Heel Of God]</char>, and he delivered them into the hands of spoilers that spoiled them, and he sold them into the hands of their enemies round about, so that they could not any longer stand before their enemies.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="15" style="v" />Whithersoever they went out, the hand of the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> was against them for evil, as the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> had said, and as the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> had sworn unto them: and they were greatly distressed.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="16" style="v" />Nevertheless the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> raised up judges, which delivered them out of the hand of those that spoiled them.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="17" style="v" />And yet they would not hearken unto their judges, but they went a whoring after other gods, and bowed themselves unto them: they turned quickly out of the way which their fathers walked in, obeying the commandments of the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char>; <char style="add">[but]</char> they did not so.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="18" style="v" />And when the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> raised them up judges, then the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> was with the judge, and delivered them out of the hand of their enemies all the days of the judge: for it repented the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> because of their groanings by reason of them that oppressed them and vexed them.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="19" style="v" />And it came to pass, when the judge was dead, <char style="add">[that]</char> they returned, and corrupted <char style="add">[themselves]</char> more than their fathers, in following other gods to serve them, and to bow down unto them; they ceased not from their own doings, nor from their stubborn way.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="20" style="v" />And the anger of the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> was hot against Yisra’el <char style="add">[He Holds Onto The Heel Of God]</char>; and he said, Because that this people has transgressed my covenant which I commanded their fathers, and have not listened unto my voice;</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="21" style="v" />I also will not from this time forth <char style="pn">(from now on)</char> drive out any from before them of the nations which Y’hoshua <char style="add">[Yehovah is Salvation]</char> left when he died:</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="22" style="v" />That through them I may prove Yisra’el <char style="add">[He Holds Onto The Heel Of God]</char>, whether they will keep the way of the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> to walk in it, as their fathers did keep <char style="add">[it]</char>, or not.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="23" style="v" />Therefore the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> left those nations, without driving them out hastily; neither delivered he them into the hand of Y’hoshua <char style="add">[Yehovah is Salvation]</char>.</para>
  <chapter number="3" style="c" />
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="1" style="v" />Now these <char style="add">[are]</char> the nations which the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> left, to prove Yisra’el <char style="add">[He Holds Onto The Heel Of God]</char> by them, <char style="add">[even]</char> as many <char style="add">[of Yisra’el [He Holds Onto The Heel Of God]]</char> as had not known all the wars of Kena’an <char style="add">[Merchant]</char>;</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="2" style="v" />Only that the generations of the people of Yisra’el <char style="add">[He Holds Onto The Heel Of God]</char> might know, to teach them war, at the least such as before knew nothing thereof;</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="3" style="v" />
    <char style="add">[Namely]</char>, five lords of the P’lishtim <char style="add">[Immigrants]</char>, and all the Kena’ani <char style="add">[Merchant]</char>, and the Tzidonim <char style="add">[Hunting]</char>, and the Hivi <char style="add">[Villagers]</char> that dwelt in mount L’vanon <char style="add">[Whiteness]</char>, from mount Ba’al <char style="add">[lord (a false god)]</char> between Mount Ba’al-Hermon <char style="add">[Lord of Destruction]</char> unto the entering in of Hamat <char style="add">[Fortress]</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="4" style="v" />And they were to prove Yisra’el <char style="add">[He Holds Onto The Heel Of God]</char> by them, to know whether they would hearken unto the commandments of the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char>, which he commanded their fathers by the hand of Moshe <char style="add">[He Who Draws Out Of The Waters]</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="5" style="v" />And the people of Yisra’el <char style="add">[He Holds Onto The Heel Of God]</char> dwelt among the Kena’ani <char style="add">[Merchant]</char>, Hitti <char style="add">[Terrorists]</char>, and Emori <char style="add">[Highlanders]</char>, and P’rizi <char style="add">[Dwellers in Unwalled Towns]</char>, and Hivi <char style="add">[Villagers]</char>, and Y’vusi <char style="add">[Threshers, Trampled Under Foot]</char>:</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="6" style="v" />And they took their daughters to be their wives, and gave their daughters to their sons, and served their gods.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="7" style="v" />And the people of Yisra’el <char style="add">[He Holds Onto The Heel Of God]</char> did evil in the sight of the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char>, and forgot the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> their God-Elōhīm <char style="pn">(The Living Word)</char> <char style="add">[The Many Powered]</char>, and served Ba’alim [lords (false gods)] and the groves.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="8" style="v" />Therefore the anger of the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> was hot against Yisra’el <char style="add">[He Holds Onto The Heel Of God]</char>, and he sold them into the hand of Kushan-Rish’atayim <char style="add">[Twice-Wicked Full of Darkness (A Reference to Ethiopia)]</char> king of Aram (Mesopotamia/Aram <char style="pn">(Syria)</char> <char style="add">[exalted]</char>) <char style="add">[Elevated Between the Two Rivers]</char>: and the people of Yisra’el <char style="add">[He Holds Onto The Heel Of God]</char> served Kushan-Rish’atayim <char style="add">[Twice-Wicked Full of Darkness (A Reference to Ethiopia)]</char> eight years.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="9" style="v" />And when the people of Yisra’el <char style="add">[He Holds Onto The Heel Of God]</char> cried unto the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char>, the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> raised up a deliverer to the people of Yisra’el <char style="add">[He Holds Onto The Heel Of God]</char>, who delivered them, <char style="add">[even]</char> ‘Otni’el <char style="add">[Lion of God]</char> the son of K’naz <char style="add">[Hunter]</char>, Kalev <char style="add">[Dog]</char>’s younger brother.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="10" style="v" />And the Spirit of the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> came upon him, and he judged Yisra’el <char style="add">[He Holds Onto The Heel Of God]</char>, and went out to war: and the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> delivered Kushan-Rish’atayim <char style="add">[Twice-Wicked Full of Darkness (A Reference to Ethiopia)]</char> king of Aram <char style="pn">(Mesopotamia/Aram (Syria) [exalted])</char> <char style="add">[Elevated Between the Two Rivers]</char> into his hand; and his hand prevailed against Kushan-Rish’atayim <char style="add">[Twice-Wicked Full of Darkness (A Reference to Ethiopia)]</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="11" style="v" />And the land had rest forty years. And ‘Otni’el <char style="add">[Lion of God]</char> the son of K’naz <char style="add">[Hunter]</char> died.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="12" style="v" />And the people of Yisra’el <char style="add">[He Holds Onto The Heel Of God]</char> did evil again in the sight of the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char>: and the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> strengthened ‘Eglon <char style="add">[Calf-like]</char> the king of Mo’av <char style="add">[Seed of my Father]</char> against Yisra’el <char style="add">[He Holds Onto The Heel Of God]</char>, because they had done evil in the sight of the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="13" style="v" />And he gathered unto him the children of ‘Amon <char style="add">[Inbred]</char> and ‘Amalek <char style="add">[Dweller in a Valley]</char>, and went and struck Yisra’el <char style="add">[He Holds Onto The Heel Of God]</char>, and possessed the city of palm trees.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="14" style="v" />So the people of Yisra’el <char style="add">[He Holds Onto The Heel Of God]</char> served ‘Eglon <char style="add">[Calf-like]</char> the king of Mo’av <char style="add">[Seed of my Father]</char> eighteen years.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="15" style="v" />But when the people of Yisra’el <char style="add">[He Holds Onto The Heel Of God]</char> cried unto the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char>, the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> raised them up a deliverer, Ehud [I will Give Thanks: I will be Praised] the son of Gera <char style="add">[A Grain]</char>, from the tribe of Binyamin <char style="add">[A Son of the Right Hand]</char>, a man left-handed: and by him the people of Yisra’el <char style="add">[He Holds Onto The Heel Of God]</char> sent a present unto ‘Eglon <char style="add">[Calf-like]</char> the king of Mo’av <char style="add">[Seed of my Father]</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="16" style="v" />But Ehud <char style="add">[I will Give Thanks: I will be Praised]</char> made him a dagger which had two edges, of a cubit length; and he did gird it under his clothing upon his right thigh.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="17" style="v" />And he brought the present unto ‘Eglon <char style="add">[Calf-like]</char> king of Mo’av <char style="add">[Seed of my Father]</char>: and ‘Eglon <char style="add">[Calf-like] [was]</char> a very fat man.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="18" style="v" />And when he had made an end to offer the present, he sent away the people that bore the present.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="19" style="v" />But he himself turned again from the quarries that <char style="add">[were]</char> by Gilgal <char style="add">[A Wheel, Rolling]</char>, and said, I have a secret errand unto you<char style="ord">i</char>, O king: who said, Keep silence. And all that stood by him went out from him.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="20" style="v" />And Ehud <char style="add">[I will Give Thanks: I will be Praised]</char> came unto him; and he was sitting in a summer parlour, which he had for himself alone. And Ehud <char style="add">[I will Give Thanks: I will be Praised]</char> said, I have a message from God-Elōhīm <char style="pn">(The Living Word)</char> <char style="add">[The Many Powered]</char> unto you<char style="ord">i</char>. And he arose out of <char style="add">[his]</char> seat.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="21" style="v" />And Ehud <char style="add">[I will Give Thanks: I will be Praised]</char> put forth his left hand, and took the dagger from his right thigh, and thrust it into his belly:</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="22" style="v" />And the handle also went in after the blade; and the fat closed upon the blade, so that he could not draw the dagger out of his belly; and the dirt came out.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="23" style="v" />Then Ehud <char style="add">[I will Give Thanks: I will be Praised]</char> went forth through the porch, and shut the doors of the parlour upon him, and locked them.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="24" style="v" />When he was gone out, his servants came; and when they saw that, behold, the doors of the parlour <char style="add">[were]</char> locked, they said, Surely he covers his feet in his summer chamber.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="25" style="v" />And they tarried till they were ashamed: and, behold, he opened not the doors of the parlour; therefore they took a key, and opened <char style="add">[them]</char>: and, behold, their lord <char style="add">[was]</char> fallen down dead on the earth.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="26" style="v" />And Ehud <char style="add">[I will Give Thanks: I will be Praised]</char> escaped while they tarried, and passed beyond the quarries, and escaped unto Se’irah <char style="add">[The Shaggy]</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="27" style="v" />And it came to pass, when he was come, that he blew a trumpet in the mountain of Efrayim <char style="add">[Doubly Fruitful]</char>, and the people of Yisra’el <char style="add">[He Holds Onto The Heel Of God]</char> went down with him from the mount, and he before them.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="28" style="v" />And he said unto them, Follow after me: for the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> has delivered your enemies the Mo’avi <char style="add">[of his father]</char> into your hand. And they went down after him, and took the fords of Yarden <char style="add">[Descender]</char> toward Mo’av <char style="add">[Seed of my Father]</char>, and did not allow a man to pass over.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="29" style="v" />And they killed of Mo’av <char style="add">[Seed of my Father]</char> at that time about ten thousand men, all lusty, and all men of valour; and there escaped not a man.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="30" style="v" />So Mo’av <char style="add">[Seed of my Father]</char> was subdued that day under the hand of Yisra’el <char style="add">[He Holds Onto The Heel Of God]</char>. And the land had rest eighty years.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="31" style="v" />And after him was Shamgar <char style="add">[Sword]</char> the son of ‘Anat <char style="add">[Answer]</char>, which killed of the P’lishtim <char style="add">[Immigrants]</char> six hundred men with an ox goad <char style="pn">(a pointed stick to get animals moving)</char>: and he also delivered Yisra’el <char style="add">[He Holds Onto The Heel Of God]</char>.</para>
  <chapter number="4" style="c" />
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="1" style="v" />And the people of Yisra’el <char style="add">[He Holds Onto The Heel Of God]</char> again did evil in the sight of the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char>, when Ehud <char style="add">[I will Give Thanks: I will be Praised]</char> was dead.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="2" style="v" />And the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> sold them into the hand of Yavin <char style="add">[Whom God Observes]</char> king of Kena’an <char style="add">[Merchant]</char>, that reigned in Hatzor <char style="add">[Castle]</char>; the captain of whose host <char style="add">[was]</char> Sisra [Battle Array (to put on; to clothe)], which dwelt in Haroshet-HaGoyim <char style="add">[Woodland of the Gentiles]</char> of the Gentiles.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="3" style="v" />And the people of Yisra’el <char style="add">[He Holds Onto The Heel Of God]</char> cried unto the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char>: for he had nine hundred chariots of iron; and twenty years he mightily oppressed the people of Yisra’el <char style="add">[He Holds Onto The Heel Of God]</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="4" style="v" />And D’vorah <char style="add">[Bee]</char>, a prophetess, the wife of Lapidot <char style="add">[Torches]</char>, she judged Yisra’el <char style="add">[He Holds Onto The Heel Of God]</char> at that time.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="5" style="v" />And she dwelt under the palm tree of D’vorah <char style="add">[Bee]</char> between Ramah <char style="add">[Hill]</char> and Beit-El <char style="add">[House of God]</char> in mount Efrayim <char style="add">[Doubly Fruitful]</char>: and the people of Yisra’el <char style="add">[He Holds Onto The Heel Of God]</char> came up to her for judgment.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="6" style="v" />And she sent and called Barak <char style="add">[Lightning]</char> the son of Avino’am <char style="add">[My Father is Delight]</char> out of Kedesh <char style="add">[Holy Place] [Holy Place]</char> in Naftali <char style="add">[My Wrestling]</char>, and said unto him, Has not the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> God-Elōhīm <char style="pn">(The Living Word)</char> <char style="add">[The Many Powered]</char> of Yisra’el <char style="add">[He Holds Onto The Heel Of God]</char> commanded, <char style="add">[saying]</char>, Go and draw toward mount Tavor <char style="add">[Mound]</char>, and take with you<char style="ord">i</char> ten thousand men of the children of Naftali <char style="add">[My Wrestling]</char> and of the children of Z’vulun <char style="add">[Glorious Dwelling Place]</char>?</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="7" style="v" />And I will draw unto you<char style="ord">i</char> to the river Kishon <char style="add">[Winding]</char> Sisra [Battle Array (to put on; to clothe)], the captain of Yavin <char style="add">[Whom God Observes]</char>’s army, with his chariots and his multitude; and I will deliver him into you<char style="ord">i</char> hand.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="8" style="v" />And Barak <char style="add">[Lightning]</char> said unto her, If you<char style="ord">i</char> will go with me, then I will go: but if you<char style="ord">i</char> will not go with me, <char style="add">[then]</char> I will not go.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="9" style="v" />And she said, I will surely go with you<char style="ord">i</char>: notwithstanding the journey that you<char style="ord">i</char> take shall not be for your<char style="ord">i</char> honour; for the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> shall sell Sisra <char style="add">[Battle Array (to put on; to clothe)]</char> into the hand of a woman. And D’vorah <char style="add">[Bee]</char> arose, and went with Barak <char style="add">[Lightning]</char> to Kedesh <char style="add">[Holy Place] [Holy Place]</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="10" style="v" />And Barak <char style="add">[Lightning]</char> called Z’vulun <char style="add">[Glorious Dwelling Place]</char> and Naftali <char style="add">[My Wrestling]</char> to Kedesh <char style="add">[Holy Place]</char>; and he went up with ten thousand men at his feet: and D’vorah <char style="add">[Bee]</char> went up with him.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="11" style="v" />Now Hever <char style="add">[Comrade]</char> the Kayin <char style="add">[Possession]</char>, <char style="add">[which was]</char> of the children of Hovav <char style="add">[Cherished]</char> the father in law of Moshe <char style="add">[He Who Draws Out Of The Waters]</char>, had severed himself from the Keini <char style="add">[traveling tinkers or blacksmiths]</char>, and pitched his tent unto the plain of Tza’ananim <char style="add">[Removings]</char>, which <char style="add">[is]</char> by Kedesh <char style="add">[Holy Place] [Holy Place]</char>..</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="12" style="v" />And they showed Sisra <char style="add">[Battle Array (to put on; to clothe)]</char> that Barak <char style="add">[Lightning]</char> the son of Avino’am <char style="add">[My Father is Delight]</char> was gone up to mount Tavor <char style="add">[Mound]</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="13" style="v" />And Sisra <char style="add">[Battle Array (to put on; to clothe)]</char> gathered together all his chariots, <char style="add">[even]</char> nine hundred chariots of iron, and all the people that <char style="add">[were]</char> with him, from Haroshet-HaGoyim <char style="add">[Woodland of the Gentiles]</char> unto the river of Kishon <char style="add">[Winding]</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="14" style="v" />And D’vorah <char style="add">[Bee]</char> said unto Barak <char style="add">[Lightning]</char>, Up; for this <char style="add">[is]</char> the day in which the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> has delivered Sisra <char style="add">[Battle Array (to put on; to clothe)]</char> into you<char style="ord">i</char> hand: is not the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> gone out before you<char style="ord">i</char>? So Barak <char style="add">[Lightning]</char> went down from mount Tavor <char style="add">[Mound]</char>, and ten thousand men after him.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="15" style="v" />And the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> scattered <char style="pn">(defeated in battle)</char> Sisra <char style="add">[Battle Array (to put on; to clothe)]</char>, and all <char style="add">[his]</char> chariots, and all <char style="add">[his]</char> host, with the edge of the sword before Barak <char style="add">[Lightning]</char>; so that Sisra <char style="add">[Battle Array (to put on; to clothe)]</char> lighted down off <char style="add">[his]</char> chariot, and fled away on his feet.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="16" style="v" />But Barak <char style="add">[Lightning]</char> pursued after the chariots, and after the host, unto Haroshet-HaGoyim <char style="add">[Woodland of the Gentiles]</char> of the Gentiles: and all the host of Sisra <char style="add">[Battle Array (to put on; to clothe)]</char> fell upon the edge of the sword; <char style="add">[and]</char> there was not a man left.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="17" style="v" />However Sisra <char style="add">[Battle Array (to put on; to clothe)]</char> fled away on his feet to the tent of Ya’el <char style="add">[Mountain Goat]</char> the wife of Hever <char style="add">[Comrade]</char> the Kayin <char style="add">[Possession]</char>: for <char style="add">[there was]</char> peace between Yavin <char style="add">[Whom God Observes]</char> the king of Hatzor <char style="add">[Castle]</char> and the house of Hever <char style="add">[Comrade]</char> the Keini <char style="add">[Possession]</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="18" style="v" />And Ya’el <char style="add">[Mountain Goat]</char> went out to meet Sisra <char style="add">[Battle Array (to put on; to clothe)]</char>, and said unto him, Turn in, my lord, turn in to me; fear not. And when he had turned in unto her into the tent, she covered him with a Mantle <char style="pn">(cloak; covering garment)</char> <char style="pn">(cloak)</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="19" style="v" />And he said unto her, Give me, I pray you<char style="ord">i</char>, a little water to drink; for I am thirsty. And she opened a bottle of milk, and gave him drink, and covered him.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="20" style="v" />Again he said unto her, Stand in the door of the tent, and it shall be, when any man does come and enquire of you<char style="ord">i</char>, and say, Is there any man here? that you<char style="ord">i</char> shall say, No.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="21" style="v" />Then Ya’el <char style="add">[Mountain Goat]</char>, Hever’s <char style="add">[Comrade]</char>’s wife took a nail of the tent, and took an hammer in her hand, and went softly unto him, and struck the nail into his temples, and fastened it into the ground: for he was fast asleep and weary. So he died.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="22" style="v" />And, behold, as Barak <char style="add">[Lightning]</char> pursued Sisra <char style="add">[Battle Array (to put on; to clothe)]</char>, Ya’el <char style="add">[Mountain Goat]</char> came out to meet him, and said unto him, Come, and I will show you<char style="ord">i</char> the man whom you<char style="ord">i</char> seek. And when he came into her <char style="add">[tent]</char>, behold, Sisra <char style="add">[Battle Array (to put on; to clothe)]</char> lay dead, and the nail <char style="add">[was]</char> in his temples.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="23" style="v" />So God-Elōhīm <char style="pn">(The Living Word)</char> <char style="add">[The Many Powered]</char> subdued on that day Yavin <char style="add">[Whom God Observes]</char> the king of Kena’an <char style="add">[Merchant]</char> before the people of Yisra’el <char style="add">[He Holds Onto The Heel Of God]</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="24" style="v" />And the hand of the people of Yisra’el <char style="add">[He Holds Onto The Heel Of God]</char> prospered, and prevailed against Yavin <char style="add">[Whom God Observes]</char> the king of Kena’an <char style="add">[Merchant]</char>, until they had destroyed Yavin <char style="add">[Whom God Observes]</char> king of Kena’an <char style="add">[Merchant]</char>.</para>
  <chapter number="5" style="c" />
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="1" style="v" />Then sang D’vorah <char style="add">[Bee]</char> and Barak <char style="add">[Lightning]</char> the son of Avino’am <char style="add">[My Father is Delight]</char> on that day, saying,</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="2" style="v" />Praise you<char style="ord">2f</char> the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> for the avenging of Yisra’el <char style="add">[He Holds Onto The Heel Of God]</char>, when the people willingly offered themselves.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="3" style="v" />Hear, O you<char style="ord">2f</char> kings; give ear, O you<char style="ord">2f</char> princes; I, <char style="add">[even]</char> I, will sing unto the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char>; I will sing <char style="add">[praise]</char> to the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> God-Elōhīm <char style="pn">(The Living Word)</char> <char style="add">[The Many Powered]</char> of Yisra’el <char style="add">[He Holds Onto The Heel Of God]</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="4" style="v" />LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char>, when you<char style="ord">i</char> went out of Se’ir <char style="add">[Shaggy]</char>, when you<char style="ord">i</char> marched out of the field of Edom <char style="add">[Red]</char>, the earth trembled, and the heavens dropped, the clouds also dropped water.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="5" style="v" />The mountains melted from before the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char>, <char style="add">[even]</char> that Sinai from before the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> God-Elōhīm <char style="pn">(The Living Word)</char> <char style="add">[The Many Powered]</char> of Yisra’el <char style="add">[He Holds Onto The Heel Of God]</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="6" style="v" />In the days of Shamgar <char style="add">[Sword]</char> the son of ‘Anat <char style="add">[Answer]</char>, in the days of Ya’el <char style="add">[Mountain Goat]</char>, the highways were unoccupied, and the travellers walked through byways.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="7" style="v" />
    <char style="add">[The inhabitants of]</char> the villages ceased, they ceased in Yisra’el <char style="add">[He Holds Onto The Heel Of God]</char>, until that I D’vorah <char style="add">[Bee]</char> arose, that I arose a mother in Yisra’el <char style="add">[He Holds Onto The Heel Of God]</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="8" style="v" />They chose new gods; then <char style="add">[was]</char> war in the gates: was there a shield or spear seen among forty thousand in Yisra’el <char style="add">[He Holds Onto The Heel Of God]</char>?</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="9" style="v" />My heart <char style="add">[is]</char> toward the governors of Yisra’el <char style="add">[He Holds Onto The Heel Of God]</char>, that offered themselves willingly among the people. Bless you<char style="ord">2f</char> the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="10" style="v" />Speak, you<char style="ord">2f</char> that ride on white asses, you<char style="ord">2f</char> that sit in judgment, and walk by the way.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="11" style="v" />
    <char style="add">[They that are delivered]</char> from the noise of archers in the places of drawing water, there shall they rehearse the righteous acts of the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char>, <char style="add">[even]</char> the righteous acts <char style="add">[toward the inhabitants]</char> of his villages in Yisra’el <char style="add">[He Holds Onto The Heel Of God]</char>: then shall the people of the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> go down to the gates.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="12" style="v" />Awake, awake, D’vorah <char style="add">[Bee]</char>: awake, awake, utter a song: arise, Barak <char style="add">[Lightning]</char>, and lead you<char style="ord">i</char> captivity captive, you<char style="ord">i</char> son of Avino’am <char style="add">[My Father is Delight]</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="13" style="v" />Then he made him that remains have dominion over the nobles among the people: the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> made me have dominion over the mighty.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="14" style="v" />Out of Efrayim <char style="add">[Doubly Fruitful] [was there]</char> a root of them against ‘Amalek <char style="add">[Dweller in a Valley]</char>; after you<char style="ord">i</char>, Binyamin <char style="add">[Son of the Right Hand/Strength]</char>, among you<char style="ord">i</char> people; out of Makhir <char style="add">[Sold]</char> came down governors, and out of Z’vulun <char style="add">[Glorious Dwelling Place]</char> they that handle the pen of the writer.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="15" style="v" />And the princes of Yissakhar <char style="add">[There Is Recompense] [were]</char> with D’vorah <char style="add">[Bee]</char>; even Yissakhar <char style="add">[There Is Recompense]</char>, and also Barak <char style="add">[Lightning]</char>: he was sent on foot into the valley. For the divisions of Re’uven <char style="add">[Behold a Son] [there were]</char> great thoughts of heart.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="16" style="v" />Why dwelled you<char style="ord">i</char> among the sheepfolds, to hear the bleatings of the flocks? For the divisions of Re’uven <char style="add">[Behold a Son] [there were]</char> great searchings of heart.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="17" style="v" />Gil’ad <char style="add">[Rocky Region]</char> abode beyond Yarden <char style="add">[Descender]</char>: and why did Dan <char style="add">[Judge]</char> remain in ships? Asher <char style="add">[Happy]</char> continued on the sea shore, and abode in his breaches.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="18" style="v" />Z’vulun <char style="add">[Glorious Dwelling Place]</char> and Naftali <char style="add">[My Wrestling] [were]</char> a people <char style="add">[that]</char> jeopardized their lives unto the death in the high places of the field.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="19" style="v" />The kings came <char style="add">[and]</char> fought, then fought the kings of Kena’an <char style="add">[Merchant]</char> in Ta’anakh <char style="add">[Sandy]</char> by the waters of Megiddo <char style="add">[Place of Crowds]</char>; they took no gain of money.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="20" style="v" />They fought from heaven; the stars in their courses fought against Sisra [Battle Array (to put on; to clothe)].</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="21" style="v" />The river of Kishon <char style="add">[Winding]</char> swept them away, that ancient river, the river Kishon <char style="add">[Winding]</char>. O my soul, you<char style="ord">i</char> have trampled down strength.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="22" style="v" />Then were the horsehoofs broken by the means of the pransings, the pransings of their mighty ones.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="23" style="v" />Curse you<char style="ord">2f</char> Meroz <char style="add">[Refuge]</char>, said the angel of the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char>, curse you<char style="ord">2f</char> bitterly the inhabitants thereof; because they came not to the help of the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char>, to the help of the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> against the mighty.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="24" style="v" />Blessed <char style="pn">(Favored by God; happy; prosperous)</char> above women shall Ya’el <char style="add">[Mountain Goat]</char> the wife of Hever <char style="add">[Comrade]</char> the Kayin <char style="add">[Possession]</char> be, Blessed <char style="pn">(Favored by God; happy; prosperous)</char> shall she be above women in the tent.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="25" style="v" />He asked water, <char style="add">[and]</char> she gave <char style="add">[him]</char> milk; she brought forth butter in a lordly dish.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="26" style="v" />She put her hand to the nail, and her right hand to the workmen’s hammer; and with the hammer she struck Sisra <char style="add">[Battle Array (to put on; to clothe)]</char>, she struck off his head, when she had pierced and stricken through his temples.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="27" style="v" />At her feet he bowed, he fell, he lay down: at her feet he bowed, he fell: where he bowed, there he fell down dead.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="28" style="v" />The mother of Sisra <char style="add">[Battle Array (to put on; to clothe)]</char> looked out at a window, and cried through the lattice, Why is his chariot <char style="add">[so]</char> long in coming? why wait the wheels of his chariots?</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="29" style="v" />Her wise ladies answered her, yes, she returned answer to herself,</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="30" style="v" />Have they not sped? have they <char style="add">[not]</char> divided the prey; to every man a girl <char style="add">[or]</char> two; to Sisra <char style="add">[Battle Array (to put on; to clothe)]</char> a prey of diverse colours, a prey of diverse colours of needlework, of diverse colours of needlework on both sides, <char style="add">[meet]</char> for the necks of <char style="add">[them that take]</char> the spoil <char style="pn">(plunder; prey; booty)</char>?</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="31" style="v" />So let all your<char style="ord">i</char> enemies perish, O LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char>: but <char style="add">[let]</char> them that love him <char style="add">[be]</char> as the sun when he goes forth in his might. And the land had rest forty years.</para>
  <chapter number="6" style="c" />
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="1" style="v" />And the people of Yisra’el <char style="add">[He Holds Onto The Heel Of God]</char> did evil in the sight of the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char>: and the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> delivered them into the hand of Midyan <char style="add">[Strife]</char> seven years.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="2" style="v" />And the hand of Midyan <char style="add">[Strife]</char> prevailed against Yisra’el <char style="add">[He Holds Onto The Heel Of God]</char>: <char style="add">[and]</char> because of the Midyanim <char style="add">[Strife]</char> the people of Yisra’el <char style="add">[He Holds Onto The Heel Of God]</char> made them the dens which <char style="add">[are]</char> in the mountains, and caves, and strong holds.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="3" style="v" />And <char style="add">[so]</char> it was, when Yisra’el <char style="add">[He Holds Onto The Heel Of God]</char> had sown, that the Midyanim <char style="add">[Strife]</char> came up, and the ‘Amalekim <char style="add">[Dwellers in a Valley]</char>, and the children of the east, even they came up against them;</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="4" style="v" />And they encamped against them, and destroyed the increase of the earth, till you<char style="ord">i</char> come unto ‘Azah <char style="add">[The Strong]</char>, and left no sustenance for Yisra’el <char style="add">[He Holds Onto The Heel Of God]</char>, neither sheep, nor ox, nor ass.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="5" style="v" />For they came up with their cattle and their tents, and they came as grasshoppers for multitude; <char style="add">[for]</char> both they and their camels were without number: and they entered into the land to destroy it.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="6" style="v" />And Yisra’el <char style="add">[He Holds Onto The Heel Of God]</char> was greatly impoverished because of the Midyanim <char style="add">[Strife]</char>; and the people of Yisra’el <char style="add">[He Holds Onto The Heel Of God]</char> cried unto the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="7" style="v" />And it came to pass, when the people of Yisra’el <char style="add">[He Holds Onto The Heel Of God]</char> cried unto the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> because of the Midyanim <char style="add">[Strife]</char>,</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="8" style="v" />That the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> sent a prophet unto the people of Yisra’el <char style="add">[He Holds Onto The Heel Of God]</char>, which said unto them, Thus says the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> God-Elōhīm <char style="pn">(The Living Word)</char> <char style="add">[The Many Powered]</char> of Yisra’el <char style="add">[He Holds Onto The Heel Of God]</char>, I brought you up from Mitzrayim <char style="add">[Egypt - The Narrow Place]</char>, and brought you forth out of the house of bondage;</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="9" style="v" />And I delivered you out of the hand of the Mitzri, and out of the hand of all that oppressed you, and drove them out from before you, and gave you their land;</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="10" style="v" />And I said unto you, I <char style="add">[am]</char> the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> your God-Elōhīm <char style="pn">(The Living Word)</char> <char style="add">[The Many Powered]</char>; fear not the gods of the Emori <char style="add">[Highlanders]</char>, in whose land you<char style="ord">2f</char> dwell: but you<char style="ord">2f</char> have not obeyed my voice.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="11" style="v" />And there came an angel of the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char>, and sat under an oak which <char style="add">[was]</char> in ‘Ofrah <char style="add">[Fawn]</char>, that <char style="add">[pertained]</char> unto Yo’ash <char style="add">[Given by the Lord]</char> the Avi’ezri <char style="add">[My Father is Help]</char>: and his son Gid’on <char style="add">[Hewer]</char> threshed wheat by the winepress, to hide <char style="add">[it]</char> from the Midyanim <char style="add">[Strife]</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="12" style="v" />And the angel of the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> appeared unto him, and said unto him, The LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> <char style="add">[is]</char> with you<char style="ord">i</char>, you<char style="ord">i</char> mighty man of valour.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="13" style="v" />And Gid’on <char style="add">[Hewer]</char> said unto him, Oh my Lord-Adon <char style="add">[Lord of the Earth]</char>, if the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> be with us, why then is all this befallen us? and where <char style="add">[be]</char> all his miracles which our fathers told us of, saying, Did not the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> bring us up from Mitzrayim [Egypt - The Narrow Place]? but now the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> has forsaken us, and delivered us into the hands of the Midyanim <char style="add">[Strife]</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="14" style="v" />And the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> looked upon him, and said, Go in this you<char style="ord">i</char> might, and you<char style="ord">i</char> shall save Yisra’el <char style="add">[He Holds Onto The Heel Of God]</char> from the hand of the Midyanim <char style="add">[Strife]</char>: have not I sent you<char style="ord">i</char>?</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="15" style="v" />And he said unto him, Oh my Lord-Adonai <char style="add">[Greatest Above All Things]</char>, by what means shall I save Yisra’el <char style="add">[He Holds Onto The Heel Of God]</char>? behold, my family <char style="add">[is]</char> poor in M’nasheh <char style="add">[Causing to Forget]</char>, and I <char style="add">[am]</char> the least in my father’s house.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="16" style="v" />And the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> said unto him, Surely I will be with you<char style="ord">i</char>, and you<char style="ord">i</char> shall strike the Midyanim <char style="add">[Strife]</char> as one man.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="17" style="v" />And he said unto him, If now I have found grace in you<char style="ord">i</char> sight, then show me a sign that you<char style="ord">i</char> talk with me.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="18" style="v" />Depart not hence, I pray you<char style="ord">i</char>, until I come unto you<char style="ord">i</char>, and bring forth my present, and set <char style="add">[it]</char> before you<char style="ord">i</char>. And he said, I will wait until you<char style="ord">i</char> come again.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="19" style="v" />And Gid’on <char style="add">[Hewer]</char> went in, and made ready a kid, and unleavened cakes of an eifah of flour: the flesh he put in a basket, and he put the broth in a pot, and brought <char style="add">[it]</char> out unto him under the oak, and presented <char style="add">[it]</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="20" style="v" />And the angel of God-Elōhīm <char style="pn">(The Living Word)</char> <char style="add">[The Many Powered]</char> said unto him, Take the flesh and the unleavened cakes, and lay <char style="add">[them]</char> upon this rock, and pour out the broth. And he did so.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="21" style="v" />Then the angel of the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> put forth the end of the staff that <char style="add">[was]</char> in his hand, and touched the flesh and the unleavened cakes; and there rose up fire out of the rock, and consumed the flesh and the unleavened cakes. Then the angel of the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> departed out of his sight.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="22" style="v" />And when Gid’on <char style="add">[Hewer]</char> perceived that he <char style="add">[was]</char> an angel of the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char>, Gid’on <char style="add">[Hewer]</char> said, Alas, O Lord-Adonai <char style="add">[Greatest Above All Things]</char> GOD-Yehōvih <char style="pn">(THE FATHER)</char>! for because I have seen an angel of the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> face to face.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="23" style="v" />And the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> said unto him, Peace <char style="add">[be]</char> unto you<char style="ord">i</char>; fear not: you<char style="ord">i</char> shall not die.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="24" style="v" />Then Gid’on <char style="add">[Hewer]</char> built an altar there unto the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char>, and called it Yehovah-Shalom <char style="add">[Messiah Pre-Incarnate {our} Peace]</char>: unto this day it <char style="add">[is]</char> yet in ‘Ofrah <char style="add">[Fawn]</char> of the Avi’ezri <char style="add">[My Father is Help]</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="25" style="v" />And it came to pass the same night, that the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> said unto him, Take you<char style="ord">i</char> father’s young bullock, even the second bullock of seven years old, and throw down the altar of Ba’al <char style="add">[lord (a false god)]</char> that you<char style="ord">i</char> father has, and cut down the grove that <char style="add">[is]</char> by it:</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="26" style="v" />And build an altar unto the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> you<char style="ord">i</char> God-Elōhīm <char style="pn">(The Living Word)</char> <char style="add">[The Many Powered]</char> upon the top of this rock, in the ordered place, and take the second bullock, and offer a burnt sacrifice with the wood of the grove which you<char style="ord">i</char> shall cut down.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="27" style="v" />Then Gid’on <char style="add">[Hewer]</char> took ten men of his servants, and did as the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> had said unto him: and <char style="add">[so]</char> it was, because he feared his father’s household, and the men of the city, that he could not do <char style="add">[it]</char> by day, that he did <char style="add">[it]</char> by night.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="28" style="v" />And when the men of the city arose early in the morning, behold, the altar of Ba’al <char style="add">[lord (a false god)]</char> was cast down, and the grove was cut down that <char style="add">[was]</char> by it, and the second bullock was offered upon the altar <char style="add">[that was]</char> built.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="29" style="v" />And they said one to another, Who has done this thing? And when they enquired and asked, they said, Gid’on <char style="add">[Hewer]</char> the son of Yo’ash <char style="add">[Given by the Lord]</char> has done this thing.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="30" style="v" />Then the men of the city said unto Yo’ash <char style="add">[Given by the Lord]</char>, Bring out you<char style="ord">i</char> son, that he may die: because he has cast down the altar of Ba’al <char style="add">[lord (a false god)]</char>, and because he has cut down the grove that <char style="add">[was]</char> by it.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="31" style="v" />And Yo’ash <char style="add">[Given by the Lord]</char> said unto all that stood against him, Will you<char style="ord">2f</char> plead for Ba’al <char style="add">[lord (a false god)]</char>? will you<char style="ord">2f</char> save him? he that will plead for him, let him be put to death whilst <char style="add">[it is yet]</char> morning: if he <char style="add">[be]</char> a god, let him plead for himself, because <char style="add">[one]</char> has cast down his altar.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="32" style="v" />Therefore on that day he called him Yeruba’al <char style="add">[let Ba’al defend]</char>, saying, Let Ba’al <char style="add">[lord (a false god)]</char> plead against him, because he has thrown down his altar.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="33" style="v" />Then all the Midyanim <char style="add">[Strife]</char> and the ‘Amalekim <char style="add">[Valley Dwellers]</char> and the children of the east were gathered together, and went over, and pitched in the valley of Yizre’el <char style="add">[God Sows]</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="34" style="v" />But the Spirit of the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> came upon Gid’on <char style="add">[Hewer]</char>, and he blew a trumpet; and Avi-ezer <char style="add">[My Father is Help]</char> was gathered after him.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="35" style="v" />And he sent messengers throughout all M’nasheh <char style="add">[Causing to Forget]</char>; who also was gathered after him: and he sent messengers unto Asher <char style="add">[Happy]</char>, and unto Z’vulun <char style="add">[Glorious Dwelling Place]</char>, and unto Naftali <char style="add">[My Wrestling]</char>; and they came up to meet them.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="36" style="v" />And Gid’on <char style="add">[Hewer]</char> said unto God-Elōhīm <char style="pn">(The Living Word)</char> <char style="add">[The Many Powered]</char>, If you<char style="ord">i</char> will save Yisra’el <char style="add">[He Holds Onto The Heel Of God]</char> by my hand, as you<char style="ord">i</char> have said,</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="37" style="v" />Behold, I will put a fleece of wool in the floor; <char style="add">[and]</char> if the dew be on the fleece only, and <char style="add">[it be]</char> dry upon all the earth <char style="add">[beside]</char>, then shall I know that you<char style="ord">i</char> will save Yisra’el <char style="add">[He Holds Onto The Heel Of God]</char> by my hand, as you<char style="ord">i</char> have said.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="38" style="v" />And it was so: for he rose up early on the morrow, and thrust the fleece together, and wringed the dew out of the fleece, a bowl full of water.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="39" style="v" />And Gid’on <char style="add">[Hewer]</char> said unto God-Elōhīm <char style="pn">(The Living Word)</char> <char style="add">[The Many Powered]</char>, Let not you<char style="ord">i</char> anger be hot against me, and I will speak but this once: let me prove, I pray you<char style="ord">i</char>, but this once with the fleece; let it now be dry only upon the fleece, and upon all the ground let there be dew.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="40" style="v" />And God-Elōhīm <char style="pn">(The Living Word)</char> <char style="add">[The Many Powered]</char> did so that night: for it was dry upon the fleece only, and there was dew on all the ground.</para>
  <chapter number="7" style="c" />
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="1" style="v" />Then Yeruba’al <char style="add">[let Ba’al defend]</char>, who <char style="add">[is]</char> Gid’on <char style="add">[Hewer]</char>, and all the people that <char style="add">[were]</char> with him, rose up early, and pitched beside the well of ‘Ein-Harod <char style="add">[spring of Herod (fear)]</char>: so that the host of the Midyanim <char style="add">[Strife]</char> were on the north side of them, by Giv’at-Moreh <char style="add">[Hill of Teacher]</char>, in the valley.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="2" style="v" />And the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> said unto Gid’on <char style="add">[Hewer]</char>, The people that <char style="add">[are]</char> with you<char style="ord">i</char> <char style="add">[are]</char> too many for me to give the Midyanim <char style="add">[Strife]</char> into their hands, lest Yisra’el <char style="add">[He Holds Onto The Heel Of God]</char> vaunt themselves against me, saying, Mine own hand has saved me.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="3" style="v" />Now therefore come <char style="pn">(let us begin!)</char>, proclaim in the ears of the people, saying, Whosoever <char style="add">[is]</char> fearful and afraid, let him return and depart early from mount Gil’ad <char style="add">[Rocky Region]</char>. And there returned of the people twenty and two thousand; and there remained ten thousand.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="4" style="v" />And the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> said unto Gid’on <char style="add">[Hewer]</char>, The people <char style="add">[are]</char> yet <char style="add">[too]</char> many; bring them down unto the water, and I will try them for you<char style="ord">i</char> there: and it shall be, <char style="add">[that]</char> of whom I say unto you<char style="ord">i</char>, This shall go with you<char style="ord">i</char>, the same shall go with you<char style="ord">i</char>; and of whomsoever I say unto you<char style="ord">i</char>, This shall not go with you<char style="ord">i</char>, the same shall not go.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="5" style="v" />So he brought down the people unto the water: and the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> said unto Gid’on <char style="add">[Hewer]</char>, Every one that laps of the water with his tongue, as a dog laps, him shall you<char style="ord">i</char> set by himself; likewise everyone that bows down upon his knees to drink.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="6" style="v" />And the number of them that lapped, <char style="add">[putting]</char> their hand to their mouth, were three hundred men: but all the rest of the people bowed down upon their knees to drink water.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="7" style="v" />And the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> said unto Gid’on <char style="add">[Hewer]</char>, By the three hundred men that lapped will I save you, and deliver the Midyanim <char style="add">[Strife]</char> into you<char style="ord">i</char> hand: and let all the <char style="add">[other]</char> people go every man unto his place.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="8" style="v" />So the people took victuals <char style="pn">(food for humans)</char> in their hand, and their trumpets: and he sent all <char style="add">[the rest of]</char> Yisra’el <char style="add">[He Holds Onto The Heel Of God]</char> every man unto his tent, and retained those three hundred men: and the host of Midyan <char style="add">[Strife]</char> was beneath him in the valley.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="9" style="v" />And it came to pass the same night, that the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> said unto him, Arise, get you<char style="ord">i</char> down unto the host; for I have delivered it into you<char style="ord">i</char> hand.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="10" style="v" />But if you<char style="ord">i</char> fear to go down, go you<char style="ord">i</char> with Purah <char style="add">[Bough]</char> you<char style="ord">i</char> servant down to the host:</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="11" style="v" />And you<char style="ord">i</char> shall hear what they say; and afterward shall you<char style="ord">i</char> hands be strengthened to go down unto the host. Then went he down with Purah <char style="add">[Bough]</char> his servant unto the outside of the armed men that <char style="add">[were]</char> in the host.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="12" style="v" />And the Midyanim <char style="add">[Strife]</char> and the ‘Amalekim <char style="add">[Dwellers in a Valley]</char> and all the children of the east lay along in the valley like grasshoppers for multitude; and their camels <char style="add">[were]</char> without number, as the sand by the sea side for multitude.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="13" style="v" />And when Gid’on <char style="add">[Hewer]</char> was come, behold, <char style="add">[there was]</char> a man that told a dream unto his fellow, and said, Behold, I dreamed a dream, and, lo, a cake of barley bread tumbled into the host of Midyan <char style="add">[Strife]</char>, and came unto a tent, and struck it that it fell, and overturned it, that the tent lay along.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="14" style="v" />And his fellow answered and said, This <char style="add">[is]</char> nothing else save the sword of Gid’on <char style="add">[Hewer]</char> the son of Yo’ash <char style="add">[Given by the Lord]</char>, a man of Yisra’el <char style="add">[He Holds Onto The Heel Of God]</char>: <char style="add">[for]</char> into his hand has God-Elōhīm <char style="pn">(The Living Word)</char> <char style="add">[The Many Powered]</char> delivered Midyan <char style="add">[Strife]</char>, and all the host.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="15" style="v" />And it was <char style="add">[so]</char>, when Gid’on <char style="add">[Hewer]</char> heard the telling of the dream, and the interpretation thereof, that he worshipped, and returned into the host of Yisra’el <char style="add">[He Holds Onto The Heel Of God]</char>, and said, Arise; for the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> has delivered into your hand the host of Midyan <char style="add">[Strife]</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="16" style="v" />And he divided the three hundred men <char style="add">[into]</char> three companies, and he put a trumpet in every man’s hand, with empty pitchers, and lamps within the pitchers.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="17" style="v" />And he said unto them, Look on me, and do likewise: and, behold, when I come to the outside of the camp, it shall be <char style="add">[that]</char>, as I do, so shall you<char style="ord">2f</char> do.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="18" style="v" />When I blow with a trumpet, I and all that <char style="add">[are]</char> with me, then blow you<char style="ord">2f</char> the trumpets also on every side of all the camp, and say, <char style="add">[The sword]</char> of the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char>, and of Gid’on <char style="add">[Hewer]</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="19" style="v" />So Gid’on <char style="add">[Hewer]</char>, and the hundred men that <char style="add">[were]</char> with him, came unto the outside of the camp in the beginning of the middle watch; and they had but newly set the watch: and they blew the trumpets, and broke the pitchers that <char style="add">[were]</char> in their hands.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="20" style="v" />And the three companies blew the trumpets, and broke the pitchers, and held the lamps in their left hands, and the trumpets in their right hands to blow <char style="add">[withal]</char>: and they cried, The sword of the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char>, and of Gid’on <char style="add">[Hewer]</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="21" style="v" />And they stood every man in his place round about the camp: and all the host ran, and cried, and fled.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="22" style="v" />And the three hundred blew the trumpets, and the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> set every man’s sword against his fellow, even throughout all the host: and the host fled to Beit-Sheetah <char style="add">[House of the Acacia Tree]</char> in Tz’rerah <char style="add">[Oppression]</char>, <char style="add">[and]</char> to the border of Avel-M’cholah <char style="add">[Meadow of Dancing]</char>, unto Tabat <char style="add">[Celebrated]</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="23" style="v" />And the men of Yisra’el <char style="add">[He Holds Onto The Heel Of God]</char> gathered themselves together out of Naftali <char style="add">[My Wrestling]</char>, and out of Asher <char style="add">[Happy]</char>, and out of all M’nasheh <char style="add">[Causing to Forget]</char>, and pursued after the Midyanim <char style="add">[Strife]</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="24" style="v" />And Gid’on <char style="add">[Hewer]</char> sent messengers throughout all mount Efrayim <char style="add">[Doubly Fruitful]</char>, saying, Come down against the Midyanim <char style="add">[Strife]</char>, and take before them the waters unto Beit-Barah <char style="add">[House of (the) Ford]</char> and Yarden <char style="add">[Descender]</char>. Then all the men of Efrayim <char style="add">[Doubly Fruitful]</char> gathered themselves together, and took the waters unto Beit-Barah <char style="add">[House of (the) Ford]</char> and Yarden <char style="add">[Descender]</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="25" style="v" />And they took two princes of the Midyanim <char style="add">[Strife]</char>, ‘Orev <char style="add">[Raven]</char> and Ze’ev <char style="add">[Wolf]</char>; and they killed ‘Orev <char style="add">[Raven]</char> upon the rock ‘Orev <char style="add">[Raven]</char>, and Ze’ev <char style="add">[Wolf]</char> they killed at the winepress of Ze’ev <char style="add">[Wolf]</char>, and pursued Midyan <char style="add">[Strife]</char>, and brought the heads of ‘Orev <char style="add">[Raven]</char> and Ze’ev <char style="add">[Wolf]</char> to Gid’on <char style="add">[Hewer]</char> on the other side Yarden <char style="add">[Descender]</char>.</para>
  <chapter number="8" style="c" />
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="1" style="v" />And the men of Efrayim <char style="add">[Doubly Fruitful]</char> said unto him, Why have you<char style="ord">i</char> served us thus, that you<char style="ord">i</char> called us not, when you<char style="ord">i</char> went to fight with the Midyanim <char style="add">[Strife]</char>? And they did quarrel with him sharply.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="2" style="v" />And he said unto them, What have I done now in comparison of you? <char style="add">[Is]</char> not the gleaning of the grapes of Efrayim <char style="add">[Doubly Fruitful]</char> better than the vintage of Avi-ezer <char style="add">[My Father is Help]</char>?</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="3" style="v" />God-Elōhīm <char style="pn">(The Living Word)</char> <char style="add">[The Many Powered]</char> has delivered into your hands the princes of Midyan <char style="add">[Strife]</char>, ‘Orev <char style="add">[Raven]</char> and Ze’ev <char style="add">[Wolf]</char>: and what was I able to do in comparison of you? Then their anger was abated toward him, when he had said that.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="4" style="v" />And Gid’on <char style="add">[Hewer]</char> came to Yarden <char style="add">[Descender]</char>, <char style="add">[and]</char> passed over, he, and the three hundred men that <char style="add">[were]</char> with him, faint, yet pursuing <char style="add">[them]</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="5" style="v" />And he said unto the men of Sukkot <char style="add">[Booths]</char>, Give, I pray you, loaves of bread unto the people that follow me; for they <char style="add">[be]</char> faint, and I am pursuing after Zevach <char style="add">[Deprived of Protection]</char> and Tzalmuna <char style="add">[Deprived of Protection]</char>, kings of Midyan <char style="add">[Strife]</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="6" style="v" />And the princes of Sukkot <char style="add">[Booths]</char> said, <char style="add">[Are]</char> the hands of Zevach <char style="add">[Deprived of Protection]</char> and Tzalmuna <char style="add">[Deprived of Protection]</char> now in you<char style="ord">i</char> hand, that we should give bread unto you<char style="ord">i</char> army?</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="7" style="v" />And Gid’on <char style="add">[Hewer]</char> said, Therefore when the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> has delivered Zevach <char style="add">[Deprived of Protection]</char> and Tzalmuna <char style="add">[Deprived of Protection]</char> into my hand, then I will tear your flesh with the thorns of the wilderness and with briers.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="8" style="v" />And he went up there to P’nu’el <char style="add">[Facing God]</char>, and spoke unto them likewise: and the men of P’nu’el <char style="add">[Facing God]</char> answered him as the men of Sukkot <char style="add">[Booths]</char> had answered <char style="add">[him]</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="9" style="v" />And he spoke also unto the men of P’nu’el <char style="add">[Facing God]</char>, saying, When I come again in peace, I will break down this tower.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="10" style="v" />Now Zevach <char style="add">[Deprived of Protection]</char> and Tzalmuna <char style="add">[Deprived of Protection] [were]</char> in Karkor <char style="add">[Foundation]</char>, and their hosts with them, about fifteen thousand <char style="add">[men]</char>, all that were left of all the hosts of the children of the east: for there fell an hundred and twenty thousand men that drew sword.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="11" style="v" />And Gid’on <char style="add">[Hewer]</char> went up by the way of them that dwelt in tents on the east of Novach <char style="add">[Barking]</char> and Yogbehah <char style="add">[Lofty]</char>, and struck the host: for the host was secure.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="12" style="v" />And when Zevach <char style="add">[Deprived of Protection]</char> and Tzalmuna <char style="add">[Deprived of Protection]</char> fled, he pursued after them, and took the two kings of Midyan <char style="add">[Strife]</char>, Zevach <char style="add">[Deprived of Protection]</char> and Tzalmuna <char style="add">[Deprived of Protection]</char>, and scattered <char style="pn">(defeated in battle)</char> all the host.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="13" style="v" />And Gid’on <char style="add">[Hewer]</char> the son of Yo’ash <char style="add">[Given by the Lord]</char> returned from battle before the sun <char style="add">[was up]</char>,</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="14" style="v" />And caught a young man of the men of Sukkot <char style="add">[Booths]</char>, and enquired of him: and he described unto him the princes of Sukkot <char style="add">[Booths]</char>, and the elders thereof, <char style="add">[even]</char> threescore and seventeen men.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="15" style="v" />And he came unto the men of Sukkot <char style="add">[Booths]</char>, and said, Behold Zevach <char style="add">[Deprived of Protection]</char> and Tzalmuna <char style="add">[Deprived of Protection]</char>, with whom you<char style="ord">2f</char> did upbraid me, saying, <char style="add">[Are]</char> the hands of Zevach <char style="add">[Deprived of Protection]</char> and Tzalmuna <char style="add">[Deprived of Protection]</char> now in you<char style="ord">i</char> hand, that we should give bread unto you<char style="ord">i</char> men <char style="add">[that are]</char> weary?</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="16" style="v" />And he took the elders of the city, and thorns of the wilderness and briers, and with them he taught the men of Sukkot <char style="add">[Booths]</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="17" style="v" />And he beat down the tower of P’nu’el <char style="add">[Facing God]</char>, and killed the men of the city.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="18" style="v" />Then said he unto Zevach <char style="add">[Deprived of Protection]</char> and Tzalmuna <char style="add">[Deprived of Protection]</char>, What manner of men <char style="add">[were they]</char> whom you<char style="ord">2f</char> killed at Tavor <char style="add">[Mound]</char>? And they answered, As you<char style="ord">i</char> <char style="add">[are]</char>, so <char style="add">[were]</char> they; each one resembled the children of a king.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="19" style="v" />And he said, They <char style="add">[were]</char> my brethren, <char style="add">[even]</char> the sons of my mother: <char style="add">[as]</char> the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> lives, if you<char style="ord">2f</char> had saved them alive, I would not slay you.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="20" style="v" />And he said unto Yeter <char style="add">[abundance]</char> his firstborn, Up, <char style="add">[and]</char> slay them. But the youth drew not his sword: for he feared, because he <char style="add">[was]</char> yet a youth.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="21" style="v" />Then Zevach <char style="add">[Deprived of Protection]</char> and Tzalmuna <char style="add">[Deprived of Protection]</char> said, Rise you<char style="ord">i</char>, and fall upon us: for as the man <char style="add">[is, so is]</char> his strength. And Gid’on <char style="add">[Hewer]</char> arose, and killed Zevach <char style="add">[Deprived of Protection]</char> and Tzalmuna <char style="add">[Deprived of Protection]</char>, and took away the ornaments that <char style="add">[were]</char> on their camels’ necks.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="22" style="v" />Then the men of Yisra’el <char style="add">[He Holds Onto The Heel Of God]</char> said unto Gid’on <char style="add">[Hewer]</char>, Rule you<char style="ord">i</char> over us, both you<char style="ord">i</char>, and you<char style="ord">i</char> son, and you<char style="ord">i</char> son’s son also: for you<char style="ord">i</char> have delivered us from the hand of Midyan <char style="add">[Strife]</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="23" style="v" />And Gid’on <char style="add">[Hewer]</char> said unto them, I will not rule over you, neither shall my son rule over you: the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> shall rule over you.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="24" style="v" />And Gid’on <char style="add">[Hewer]</char> said unto them, I would desire a request of you, that you<char style="ord">2f</char> would give me every man the earrings of his prey. (For they had golden earrings, because they <char style="add">[were]</char> Yishma’elim <char style="pn">(Ishmaelites)</char> <char style="add">[God will Hear]</char>.)</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="25" style="v" />And they answered, We will willingly give <char style="add">[them]</char>. And they spread a garment, and did cast in it every man the earrings of his prey.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="26" style="v" />And the weight of the golden earrings that he requested was a thousand and seven hundred <char style="add">[shekels]</char> of gold; beside ornaments, and collars, and purple clothing that <char style="add">[was]</char> on the kings of Midyan <char style="add">[Strife]</char>, and beside the chains that <char style="add">[were]</char> about their camels’ necks.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="27" style="v" />And Gid’on <char style="add">[Hewer]</char> made an ephod <char style="pn">(vest)</char> thereof, and put it in his city, <char style="add">[even]</char> in ‘Ofrah <char style="add">[Fawn]</char>: and all Yisra’el <char style="add">[He Holds Onto The Heel Of God]</char> went there a whoring after it: which thing became a snare unto Gid’on <char style="add">[Hewer]</char>, and to his house.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="28" style="v" />Thus was Midyan <char style="add">[Strife]</char> subdued before the people of Yisra’el <char style="add">[He Holds Onto The Heel Of God]</char>, so that they lifted up their heads no more. And the country was in quietness forty years in the days of Gid’on <char style="add">[Hewer]</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="29" style="v" />And Yeruba’al <char style="add">[let Ba’al defend]</char> the son of Yo’ash <char style="add">[Given by the Lord]</char> went and dwelt in his own house.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="30" style="v" />And Gid’on <char style="add">[Hewer]</char> had threescore and ten sons of his body begotten: for he had many wives.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="31" style="v" />And his concubine that <char style="add">[was]</char> in Sh’khem <char style="add">[Shoulder]</char>, she also bore him a son, whose name he called Avi-Melekh <char style="add">[My Father is King]</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="32" style="v" />And Gid’on <char style="add">[Hewer]</char> the son of Yo’ash <char style="add">[Given by the Lord]</char> died in a good old age, and was buried in the sepulcher of Yo’ash <char style="add">[Given by the Lord]</char> his father, in ‘Ofrah <char style="add">[Fawn]</char> of the Avi’ezri <char style="add">[My Father is Help]</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="33" style="v" />And it came to pass, as soon as Gid’on <char style="add">[Hewer]</char> was dead, that the people of Yisra’el <char style="add">[He Holds Onto The Heel Of God]</char> turned again, and went a whoring after Ba’alim <char style="add">[lords (false gods)]</char>, and made Ba’al-B’rit <char style="add">[lord of the covenant]</char> their god.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="34" style="v" />And the people of Yisra’el <char style="add">[He Holds Onto The Heel Of God]</char> remembered not the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> their God-Elōhīm <char style="pn">(The Living Word)</char> <char style="add">[The Many Powered]</char>, who had delivered them out of the hands of all their enemies on every side:</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="35" style="v" />Neither showed they kindness to the house of Yeruba’al <char style="add">[let Ba’al defend]</char>, <char style="add">[namely]</char>, Gid’on <char style="add">[Hewer]</char>, according to all the goodness which he had showed unto Yisra’el <char style="add">[He Holds Onto The Heel Of God]</char>.</para>
  <chapter number="9" style="c" />
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="1" style="v" />And Avi-Melekh <char style="add">[My Father is King]</char> the son of Yeruba’al <char style="add">[let Ba’al defend]</char> went to Sh’khem <char style="add">[Shoulder]</char> unto his mother’s brethren, and communed with them, and with all the family of the house of his mother’s father, saying,</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="2" style="v" />Speak, I pray you, in the ears of all the men of Sh’khem <char style="add">[Shoulder]</char>, Whether <char style="add">[is]</char> better for you, either that all the sons of Yeruba’al <char style="add">[let Ba’al defend]</char>, <char style="add">[which are]</char> threescore and ten persons, reign over you, or that one reign over you? remember also that I <char style="add">[am]</char> your bone and your flesh.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="3" style="v" />And his mother’s brethren spoke of him in the ears of all the men of Sh’khem <char style="add">[Shoulder]</char> all these words: and their hearts inclined to follow Avi-Melekh <char style="add">[My Father is King]</char>; for they said, He <char style="add">[is]</char> our brother.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="4" style="v" />And they gave him threescore and ten <char style="add">[pieces]</char> of silver out of the house of Ba’al-B’rit <char style="add">[lord of the covenant]</char>, which Avi-Melekh <char style="add">[My Father is King]</char> hired vain and light persons, which followed him.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="5" style="v" />And he went unto his father’s house at ‘Ofrah <char style="add">[Fawn]</char>, and killed his brethren the sons of Yeruba’al <char style="add">[let Ba’al defend]</char>, <char style="add">[being]</char> threescore and ten persons, upon one stone: notwithstanding yet Toram <char style="add">[Yehovah is Perfect]</char> the youngest son of Yeruba’al [let Ba’al defend] was left; for he hid himself.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="6" style="v" />And all the men of Sh’khem <char style="add">[Shoulder]</char> gathered together, and all the Beit-Millo <char style="add">[fortification (defensive structure) or mound] [House of the Fortification (defensive structure)]</char>, and went, and made Avi-Melekh <char style="add">[My Father is King]</char> king, by the plain of the pillar that <char style="add">[was]</char> in Sh’khem <char style="add">[Shoulder]</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="7" style="v" />And when they told <char style="add">[it]</char> to Toram <char style="add">[Yehovah is Perfect]</char>, he went and stood in the top of mount G’rizim <char style="add">[Cuttings Off]</char>, and lifted up his voice, and cried, and said unto them, Listen unto me, you<char style="ord">2f</char> men of Sh’khem <char style="add">[Shoulder]</char>, that God-Elōhīm <char style="pn">(The Living Word)</char> <char style="add">[The Many Powered]</char> may hearken unto you.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="8" style="v" />The trees went forth <char style="add">[on a time]</char> to anoint a king over them; and they said unto the olive tree, Reign you<char style="ord">i</char> over us.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="9" style="v" />But the olive tree said unto them, Should I leave my fatness, which by me they honour God-Elōhīm <char style="pn">(The Living Word)</char> <char style="add">[The Many Powered]</char> and man, and go to be promoted over the trees?</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="10" style="v" />And the trees said to the fig tree, Come you<char style="ord">i</char>, <char style="add">[and]</char> reign over us.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="11" style="v" />But the fig tree said unto them, Should I forsake my sweetness, and my good fruit, and go to be promoted over the trees?</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="12" style="v" />Then said the trees unto the vine, Come you<char style="ord">i</char>, <char style="add">[and]</char> reign over us.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="13" style="v" />And the vine said unto them, Should I leave my wine, which cheers God-Elōhīm <char style="pn">(The Living Word)</char> <char style="add">[The Many Powered]</char> and man, and go to be promoted over the trees?</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="14" style="v" />Then said all the trees unto the bramble, Come you<char style="ord">i</char>, <char style="add">[and]</char> reign over us.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="15" style="v" />And the bramble said unto the trees, If in tyou<char style="ord">2f</char> anoint me king over you, <char style="add">[then]</char> come <char style="add">[and]</char> put your trust in my shadow: and if not, let fire come out of the bramble, and devour the cedars of L’vanon <char style="add">[Whiteness]</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="16" style="v" />Now therefore, if you<char style="ord">2f</char> have done truly and sincerely, in that you<char style="ord">2f</char> have made Avi-Melekh <char style="add">[My Father is King]</char> king, and if you<char style="ord">2f</char> have dealt well with Yeruba’al [let Ba’al defend] and his house, and have done unto him according to the deserving of his hands;</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="17" style="v" />(For my father fought for you, and adventured his life far, and delivered you out of the hand of Midyan <char style="add">[Strife]</char>:</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="18" style="v" />And you<char style="ord">2f</char> are risen up against my father’s house this day, and have slain his sons, threescore and ten persons, upon one stone, and have made Avi-Melekh <char style="add">[My Father is King]</char>, the son of his maidservant, king over the men of Sh’khem <char style="add">[Shoulder]</char>, because he <char style="add">[is]</char> your brother;)</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="19" style="v" />If you<char style="ord">2f</char> then have dealt truly and sincerely with Yeruba’al [let Ba’al defend] and with his house this day, <char style="add">[then]</char> rejoice you<char style="ord">2f</char> in Avi-Melekh <char style="add">[My Father is King]</char>, and let him also rejoice in you:</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="20" style="v" />But if not, let fire come out from Avi-Melekh <char style="add">[My Father is King]</char>, and devour the men of Sh’khem <char style="add">[Shoulder]</char>, and the Beit-Millo [fortification <char style="pn">(defensive structure)</char> or mound] <char style="add">[House of the Fortification (defensive structure)]</char>; and let fire come out from the men of Sh’khem <char style="add">[Shoulder]</char>, and from the Beit-Millo [fortification <char style="pn">(defensive structure)</char> or mound] <char style="add">[House of the Fortification (defensive structure)]</char>, and devour Avi-Melekh <char style="add">[My Father is King]</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="21" style="v" />And Toram <char style="add">[Yehovah is Perfect]</char> ran away, and fled, and went to Be’er <char style="add">[Well]</char>, and dwelt there, for fear of Avi-Melekh <char style="add">[My Father is King]</char> his brother.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="22" style="v" />When Avi-Melekh <char style="add">[My Father is King]</char> had reigned three years over Yisra’el <char style="add">[He Holds Onto The Heel Of God]</char>,</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="23" style="v" />Then God-Elōhīm <char style="pn">(The Living Word)</char> <char style="add">[The Many Powered]</char> sent an evil spirit between Avi-Melekh <char style="add">[My Father is King]</char> and the men of Sh’khem <char style="add">[Shoulder]</char>; and the men of Sh’khem <char style="add">[Shoulder]</char> dealt treacherously with Avi-Melekh <char style="add">[My Father is King]</char>:</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="24" style="v" />That the cruelty <char style="add">[done]</char> to the threescore and ten sons of Yeruba’al [let Ba’al defend] might come, and their blood be laid upon Avi-Melekh <char style="add">[My Father is King]</char> their brother, which killed them; and upon the men of Sh’khem <char style="add">[Shoulder]</char>, which aided him in the killing of his brethren.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="25" style="v" />And the men of Sh’khem <char style="add">[Shoulder]</char> set liers in wait for him in the top of the mountains, and they robbed all that came along that way by them: and it was told Avi-Melekh <char style="add">[My Father is King]</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="26" style="v" />And Ga’al <char style="add">[Loathing]</char> the son of Eved <char style="add">[A Slave]</char> came with his brethren, and went over to Sh’khem <char style="add">[Shoulder]</char>: and the men of Sh’khem <char style="add">[Shoulder]</char> put their confidence in him.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="27" style="v" />And they went out into the fields, and gathered their vineyards, and trampled <char style="add">[the grapes]</char>, and made merry, and went into the house of their god, and did eat and drink, and cursed Avi-Melekh <char style="add">[My Father is King]</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="28" style="v" />And Ga’al <char style="add">[Loathing]</char> the son of Eved <char style="add">[A Slave]</char> said, Who <char style="add">[is]</char> Avi-Melekh <char style="add">[My Father is King]</char>, and who <char style="add">[is]</char> Sh’khem <char style="add">[Shoulder]</char>, that we should serve him? <char style="add">[is]</char> not <char style="add">[he]</char> the son of Yeruba’al <char style="add">[let Ba’al defend]</char>? and Z’vul <char style="add">[Exalted]</char> his officer? serve the men of Hamor <char style="add">[male-donkey (ass)]</char> the father of Sh’khem <char style="add">[Shoulder]</char>: for why should we serve him?</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="29" style="v" />And would to God-Elōhīm <char style="pn">(The Living Word)</char> <char style="add">[The Many Powered]</char> this people were under my hand! then would I remove Avi-Melekh <char style="add">[My Father is King]</char>. And he said to Avi-Melekh <char style="add">[My Father is King]</char>, Increase you<char style="ord">i</char> army, and come out.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="30" style="v" />And when Z’vul <char style="add">[Exalted]</char> the ruler of the city heard the words of Ga’al <char style="add">[Loathing]</char> the son of Eved <char style="add">[A Slave]</char>, his anger was kindled.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="31" style="v" />And he sent messengers unto Avi-Melekh <char style="add">[My Father is King]</char> privately, saying, Behold, Ga’al <char style="add">[Loathing]</char> the son of Eved <char style="add">[A Slave]</char> and his brethren be come to Sh’khem <char style="add">[Shoulder]</char>; and, behold, they fortify the city against you<char style="ord">i</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="32" style="v" />Now therefore up by night, you<char style="ord">i</char> and the people that <char style="add">[is]</char> with you<char style="ord">i</char>, and lie in wait in the field:</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="33" style="v" />And it shall be, <char style="add">[that]</char> in the morning, as soon as the sun is up, you<char style="ord">i</char> shall rise early, and set upon the city: and, behold, <char style="add">[when]</char> he and the people that <char style="add">[is]</char> with him come out against you<char style="ord">i</char>, then may you<char style="ord">i</char> do to them as you<char style="ord">i</char> shall find occasion.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="34" style="v" />And Avi-Melekh <char style="add">[My Father is King]</char> rose up, and all the people that <char style="add">[were]</char> with him, by night, and they laid wait against Sh’khem <char style="add">[Shoulder]</char> in four companies.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="35" style="v" />And Ga’al <char style="add">[Loathing]</char> the son of Eved <char style="add">[A Slave]</char> went out, and stood in the entering of the gate of the city: and Avi-Melekh <char style="add">[My Father is King]</char> rose up, and the people that <char style="add">[were]</char> with him, from lying in wait.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="36" style="v" />And when Ga’al <char style="add">[Loathing]</char> saw the people, he said to Z’vul <char style="add">[Exalted]</char>, Behold, there come people down from the top of the mountains. And Z’vul <char style="add">[Exalted]</char> said unto him, you<char style="ord">i</char> see the shadow of the mountains as <char style="add">[if they were]</char> men.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="37" style="v" />And Ga’al <char style="add">[Loathing]</char> spoke again and said, See there come people down by the middle of the land, and another company come along by the plain of M’on’nim <char style="add">[Fortune Teller]</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="38" style="v" />Then said Z’vul <char style="add">[Exalted]</char> unto him, Where <char style="add">[is]</char> now you<char style="ord">i</char> mouth, which you<char style="ord">i</char> said, Who <char style="add">[is]</char> Avi-Melekh <char style="add">[My Father is King]</char>, that we should serve him? <char style="add">[is]</char> not this the people that you<char style="ord">i</char> have despised? go out, I pray now, and fight with them.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="39" style="v" />And Ga’al <char style="add">[Loathing]</char> went out before the men of Sh’khem <char style="add">[Shoulder]</char>, and fought with Avi-Melekh <char style="add">[My Father is King]</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="40" style="v" />And Avi-Melekh <char style="add">[My Father is King]</char> chased him, and he fled before him, and many were overthrown <char style="add">[and]</char> wounded, <char style="add">[even]</char> unto the entering of the gate.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="41" style="v" />And Avi-Melekh <char style="add">[My Father is King]</char> dwelt at Arumah: and Z’vul <char style="add">[Exalted]</char> thrust out Ga’al <char style="add">[Loathing]</char> and his brethren, that they should not dwell in Sh’khem <char style="add">[Shoulder]</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="42" style="v" />And it came to pass on the morrow, that the people went out into the field; and they told Avi-Melekh <char style="add">[My Father is King]</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="43" style="v" />And he took the people, and divided them into three companies, and laid wait in the field, and looked, and, behold, the people <char style="add">[were]</char> come forth out of the city; and he rose up against them, and struck them.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="44" style="v" />And Avi-Melekh <char style="add">[My Father is King]</char>, and the company that <char style="add">[was]</char> with him, rushed forward, and stood in the entering of the gate of the city: and the two <char style="add">[other]</char> companies ran upon all <char style="add">[the people]</char> that <char style="add">[were]</char> in the fields, and killed them.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="45" style="v" />And Avi-Melekh <char style="add">[My Father is King]</char> fought against the city all that day; and he took the city, and killed the people that <char style="add">[was]</char> in it, and beat down the city, and sowed it with salt.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="46" style="v" />And when all the men of the tower of Sh’khem <char style="add">[Shoulder]</char> heard <char style="add">[that]</char>, they entered into an hold of the temple of El-B’rit <char style="add">[(the) god Berith]</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="47" style="v" />And it was told Avi-Melekh <char style="add">[My Father is King]</char>, that all the men of the tower of Sh’khem <char style="add">[Shoulder]</char> were gathered together.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="48" style="v" />And Avi-Melekh <char style="add">[My Father is King]</char> got him up to Mount Tzalmon <char style="add">[Shady]</char>, he and all the people that <char style="add">[were]</char> with him; and Avi-Melekh <char style="add">[My Father is King]</char> took an axe in his hand, and cut down a bough from the trees, and took it, and laid <char style="add">[it]</char> on his shoulder, and said unto the people that <char style="add">[were]</char> with him, What you<char style="ord">2f</char> have seen me do, make haste, <char style="add">[and]</char> do as I <char style="add">[have done]</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="49" style="v" />And all the people likewise cut down every man his bough, and followed Avi-Melekh <char style="add">[My Father is King]</char>, and put <char style="add">[them]</char> to the hold, and set the hold on fire upon them; so that all the men of the tower of Sh’khem <char style="add">[Shoulder]</char> died also, about a thousand men and women.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="50" style="v" />Then went Avi-Melekh <char style="add">[My Father is King]</char> to Tevetz <char style="add">[Conspicuous]</char>, and encamped against Tevetz <char style="add">[Conspicuous]</char>, and took it.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="51" style="v" />But there was a strong tower within the city, and there fled all the men and women, and all they of the city, and shut <char style="add">[it]</char> to them, and got them up to the top of the tower.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="52" style="v" />And Avi-Melekh <char style="add">[My Father is King]</char> came unto the tower, and fought against it, and went hard unto the door of the tower to burn it with fire.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="53" style="v" />And a certain woman cast a piece of a millstone upon Avi-Melekh’s <char style="add">[My Father is King]</char>’s head, and all to <char style="pn">(to do entirely, do wholly)</char> broke his skull.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="54" style="v" />Then he called hastily unto the young man his armourbearer, and said unto him, Draw your<char style="ord">i</char> sword, and slay me, that men say not of me, A woman killed him. And his young man thrust him through, and he died.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="55" style="v" />And when the men of Yisra’el <char style="add">[He Holds Onto The Heel Of God]</char> saw that Avi-Melekh <char style="add">[My Father is King]</char> was dead, they departed every man unto his place.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="56" style="v" />Thus God-Elōhīm <char style="pn">(The Living Word)</char> <char style="add">[The Many Powered]</char> rendered the wickedness of Avi-Melekh <char style="add">[My Father is King]</char>, which he did unto his father, in slaying his seventy brethren:</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="57" style="v" />And all the evil of the men of Sh’khem <char style="add">[Shoulder]</char> did God-Elōhīm <char style="pn">(The Living Word)</char> <char style="add">[The Many Powered]</char> render upon their heads: and upon them came the curse of Toram <char style="add">[Yehovah is Perfect]</char> the son of Yeruba’al <char style="add">[let Ba’al defend]</char>.</para>
  <chapter number="10" style="c" />
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="1" style="v" />And after Avi-Melekh <char style="add">[My Father is King]</char> there arose to defend Yisra’el <char style="add">[He Holds Onto The Heel Of God]</char> Tola <char style="add">[worm]</char> the son of Puah <char style="add">[Splendid]</char>, the son of Dodo <char style="add">[his beloved]</char>, a man of Yissakhar <char style="add">[There Is Recompense]</char>; and he dwelt in Shamir <char style="add">[A Point or Thorn]</char> in mount Efrayim <char style="add">[Doubly Fruitful]</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="2" style="v" />And he judged Yisra’el <char style="add">[He Holds Onto The Heel Of God]</char> twenty and three years, and died, and was buried in Shamir <char style="add">[A Point or Thorn]</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="3" style="v" />And after him arose Ya’ir <char style="add">[He Enlightens]</char>, a Gil’adi <char style="add">[Hill of Testimony]</char>, and judged Yisra’el <char style="add">[He Holds Onto The Heel Of God]</char> twenty and two years.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="4" style="v" />And he had thirty sons that rode on thirty ass colts, and they had thirty cities, which are called Havot-Ya’ir <char style="add">[Villages of the Enlighteners]</char> unto this day, which <char style="add">[are]</char> in the land of Gil’ad <char style="add">[Rocky Region]</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="5" style="v" />And Ya’ir <char style="add">[He Enlightens]</char> died, and was buried in Kamon <char style="add">[Raised]</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="6" style="v" />And the people of Yisra’el <char style="add">[He Holds Onto The Heel Of God]</char> did evil again in the sight of the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char>, and served Ba’alim <char style="add">[lords (false gods)]</char>, and ‘Ashtarot <char style="add">[Star (female deity)]</char>, and the gods of Aram <char style="pn">(Aram (Syria) [exalted])</char>, and the gods of Tzidon <char style="add">[Hunting]</char>, and the gods of Mo’av <char style="add">[Seed of my Father]</char>, and the gods of the children of ‘Amon <char style="add">[Inbred]</char>, and the gods of the P’lishtim <char style="add">[Immigrants]</char>, and forsook the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char>, and served not him.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="7" style="v" />And the anger of the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> was hot against Yisra’el <char style="add">[He Holds Onto The Heel Of God]</char>, and he sold them into the hands of the P’lishtim <char style="add">[Immigrants]</char>, and into the hands of the children of ‘Amon <char style="add">[Inbred]</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="8" style="v" />And that year they vexed and oppressed the people of Yisra’el <char style="add">[He Holds Onto The Heel Of God]</char>: eighteen years, all the people of Yisra’el <char style="add">[He Holds Onto The Heel Of God]</char> that <char style="add">[were]</char> on the other side Yarden <char style="add">[Descender]</char> in the land of the Emori <char style="add">[Highlanders]</char>, which <char style="add">[is]</char> in Gil’ad <char style="add">[Rocky Region]</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="9" style="v" />Moreover the children of ‘Amon <char style="add">[Inbred]</char> passed over Yarden <char style="add">[Descender]</char> to fight also against Y’hudah <char style="add">[Let Him (God) Be Praised]</char>, and against Binyamin <char style="add">[Son of the Right Hand/Strength]</char>, and against the house of Efrayim <char style="add">[Doubly Fruitful]</char>; so that Yisra’el <char style="add">[He Holds Onto The Heel Of God]</char> was sore distressed.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="10" style="v" />And the people of Yisra’el <char style="add">[He Holds Onto The Heel Of God]</char> cried unto the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char>, saying, We have sinned against you<char style="ord">i</char>, both because we have forsaken our God-Elōhīm <char style="pn">(The Living Word)</char> <char style="add">[The Many Powered]</char>, and also served Ba’alim <char style="add">[lords (false gods)]</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="11" style="v" />And the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> said unto the people of Yisra’el <char style="add">[He Holds Onto The Heel Of God]</char>, <char style="add">[Did]</char> not <char style="add">[I deliver you]</char> from the Mitzri, and from the Emori <char style="add">[Highlanders]</char>, from the children of ‘Amon <char style="add">[Inbred]</char>, and from the P’lishtim <char style="add">[Immigrants]</char>?</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="12" style="v" />The people of Tzidon <char style="add">[Hunting]</char> also, and the ‘Amalekim <char style="add">[Dwellers in a Valley]</char>, and the Ma’on <char style="add">[Habitation]</char>, did oppress you; and you<char style="ord">2f</char> cried to me, and I delivered you out of their hand.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="13" style="v" />Yet you<char style="ord">2f</char> have forsaken me, and served other gods: wherefore I will deliver you no more.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="14" style="v" />Go and cry unto the gods which you<char style="ord">2f</char> have chosen; let them deliver you in the time of your tribulation.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="15" style="v" />And the people of Yisra’el <char style="add">[He Holds Onto The Heel Of God]</char> said unto the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char>, We have sinned: do you<char style="ord">i</char> unto us whatsoever seems good unto you<char style="ord">i</char>; deliver us only, we pray you<char style="ord">i</char>, this day.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="16" style="v" />And they put away the strange gods from among them, and served the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char>: and his soul was grieved for the misery of Yisra’el <char style="add">[He Holds Onto The Heel Of God]</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="17" style="v" />Then the children of ‘Amon <char style="add">[Inbred]</char> were gathered together, and encamped in Gil’ad <char style="add">[Rocky Region]</char>. And the people of Yisra’el <char style="add">[He Holds Onto The Heel Of God]</char> assembled themselves together, and encamped in Mitzpah <char style="add">[Watchtower]</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="18" style="v" />And the people <char style="add">[and]</char> princes of Gil’ad <char style="add">[Rocky Region]</char> said one to another, What man <char style="add">[is he]</char> that will begin to fight against the children of ‘Amon <char style="add">[Inbred]</char>? he shall be head over all the inhabitants of Gil’ad <char style="add">[Rocky Region]</char>.</para>
  <chapter number="11" style="c" />
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="1" style="v" />Now Yiftach <char style="add">[He Opens]</char> the Gil’adi <char style="add">[Hill of Testimony]</char> was a mighty man of valour, and he <char style="add">[was]</char> the son of an prostitute: and Gil’ad <char style="add">[Rocky Region]</char> begat <char style="pn">(to be father of; be ancestor of)</char> Yiftach <char style="add">[He Opens]</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="2" style="v" />And Gil’ad <char style="add">[Rocky Region]</char>’s wife bore him sons; and his wife’s sons grew up, and they thrust out Yiftach <char style="add">[He Opens]</char>, and said unto him, you<char style="ord">i</char> shall not inherit in our father’s house; for you<char style="ord">i</char> <char style="add">[are]</char> the son of a strange woman.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="3" style="v" />Then Yiftach <char style="add">[He Opens]</char> fled from his brethren, and dwelt in the land of Tov <char style="add">[Good]</char>: and there were gathered vain men to Yiftach <char style="add">[He Opens]</char>, and went out with him.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="4" style="v" />And it came to pass in process of time, that the children of ‘Amon <char style="add">[Inbred]</char> made war against Yisra’el <char style="add">[He Holds Onto The Heel Of God]</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="5" style="v" />And it was so, that when the children of ‘Amon <char style="add">[Inbred]</char> made war against Yisra’el <char style="add">[He Holds Onto The Heel Of God]</char>, the elders of Gil’ad <char style="add">[Rocky Region]</char> went to fetch Yiftach <char style="add">[He Opens]</char> out of the land of Tov <char style="add">[Good]</char>:</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="6" style="v" />And they said unto Yiftach <char style="add">[He Opens]</char>, Come, and be our captain, that we may fight with the children of ‘Amon <char style="add">[Inbred]</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="7" style="v" />And Yiftach <char style="add">[He Opens]</char> said unto the elders of Gil’ad <char style="add">[Rocky Region]</char>, Did not you<char style="ord">2f</char> hate me, and expel me out of my father’s house? and why are you<char style="ord">2f</char> come unto me now when you<char style="ord">2f</char> are in distress?</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="8" style="v" />And the elders of Gil’ad <char style="add">[Rocky Region]</char> said unto Yiftach <char style="add">[He Opens]</char>, Therefore we turn again to you<char style="ord">i</char> now, that you<char style="ord">i</char> may go with us, and fight against the children of ‘Amon <char style="add">[Inbred]</char>, and be our head over all the inhabitants of Gil’ad <char style="add">[Rocky Region]</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="9" style="v" />And Yiftach <char style="add">[He Opens]</char> said unto the elders of Gil’ad <char style="add">[Rocky Region]</char>, If you<char style="ord">2f</char> bring me home again to fight against the children of ‘Amon <char style="add">[Inbred]</char>, and the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> deliver them before me, shall I be your head?</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="10" style="v" />And the elders of Gil’ad <char style="add">[Rocky Region]</char> said unto Yiftach <char style="add">[He Opens]</char>, The LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> be witness between us, if we do not so according to you<char style="ord">i</char> words.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="11" style="v" />Then Yiftach <char style="add">[He Opens]</char> went with the elders of Gil’ad <char style="add">[Rocky Region]</char>, and the people made him head and captain over them: and Yiftach <char style="add">[He Opens]</char> uttered all his words before the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> in Mitzpah <char style="add">[Watchtower]</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="12" style="v" />And Yiftach <char style="add">[He Opens]</char> sent messengers unto the king of the children of ‘Amon <char style="add">[Inbred]</char>, saying, What have you<char style="ord">i</char> to do with me, that you<char style="ord">i</char> are come against me to fight in my land?</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="13" style="v" />And the king of the children of ‘Amon <char style="add">[Inbred]</char> answered unto the messengers of Yiftach <char style="add">[He Opens]</char>, Because Yisra’el <char style="add">[He Holds Onto The Heel Of God]</char> took away my land, when they came up out of Mitzrayim <char style="add">[Egypt - The Narrow Place]</char>, from ‘Arnon <char style="add">[Rushing Stream]</char> even unto Yabok <char style="add">[luxuriant emptying river]</char>, and unto Yarden <char style="add">[Descender]</char>: now therefore restore those <char style="add">[lands]</char> again peaceably.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="14" style="v" />And Yiftach <char style="add">[He Opens]</char> sent messengers again unto the king of the children of ‘Amon <char style="add">[Inbred]</char>:</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="15" style="v" />And said unto him, Thus says Yiftach <char style="add">[He Opens]</char>, Yisra’el <char style="add">[He Holds Onto The Heel Of God]</char> took not away the land of Mo’av <char style="add">[Seed of my Father]</char>, nor the land of the children of ‘Amon <char style="add">[Inbred]</char>:</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="16" style="v" />But when Yisra’el <char style="add">[He Holds Onto The Heel Of God]</char> came up from Mitzrayim <char style="add">[Egypt - The Narrow Place]</char>, and walked through the wilderness unto the Red sea, and came to Kadesh <char style="add">[Holy]</char>;</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="17" style="v" />Then Yisra’el <char style="add">[He Holds Onto The Heel Of God]</char> sent messengers unto the king of Edom <char style="add">[Red]</char>, saying, Let me, I pray you<char style="ord">i</char>, pass through you<char style="ord">i</char> land: but the king of Edom <char style="add">[Red]</char> would not hearken <char style="add">[thereto]</char>. And in like manner they sent unto the king of Mo’av <char style="add">[Seed of my Father]</char>: but he would not <char style="add">[consent]</char>: and Yisra’el <char style="add">[He Holds Onto The Heel Of God]</char> abode in Kadesh <char style="add">[Holy]</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="18" style="v" />Then they went along through the wilderness, and compassed the land of Edom <char style="add">[Red]</char>, and the land of Mo’av <char style="add">[Seed of my Father]</char>, and came by the east side of the land of Mo’av <char style="add">[Seed of my Father]</char>, and pitched on the other side of ‘Arnon <char style="add">[Rushing Stream]</char>, but came not within the border of Mo’av <char style="add">[Seed of my Father]</char>: for ‘Arnon <char style="add">[Rushing Stream] [was]</char> the border of Mo’av <char style="add">[Seed of my Father]</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="19" style="v" />And Yisra’el <char style="add">[He Holds Onto The Heel Of God]</char> sent messengers unto Sichon <char style="add">[Warrior]</char> king of the Emori <char style="add">[Highlanders]</char>, the king of Heshbon <char style="add">[Stronghold]</char>; and Yisra’el <char style="add">[He Holds Onto The Heel Of God]</char> said unto him, Let us pass, we pray you<char style="ord">i</char>, through you<char style="ord">i</char> land into my place.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="20" style="v" />But Sichon <char style="add">[Warrior]</char> trusted not Yisra’el <char style="add">[He Holds Onto The Heel Of God]</char> to pass through his coast: but Sichon <char style="add">[Warrior]</char> gathered all his people together, and pitched in Yachatz <char style="add">[Trampled Down]</char>, and fought against Yisra’el <char style="add">[He Holds Onto The Heel Of God]</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="21" style="v" />And the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> God-Elōhīm <char style="pn">(The Living Word)</char> <char style="add">[The Many Powered]</char> of Yisra’el <char style="add">[He Holds Onto The Heel Of God]</char> delivered Sichon <char style="add">[Warrior]</char> and all his people into the hand of Yisra’el <char style="add">[He Holds Onto The Heel Of God]</char>, and they struck them: so Yisra’el <char style="add">[He Holds Onto The Heel Of God]</char> possessed all the land of the Emori <char style="add">[Highlanders]</char>, the inhabitants of that country.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="22" style="v" />And they possessed all the coasts of the Emori <char style="add">[Highlanders]</char>, from ‘Arnon <char style="add">[Rushing Stream]</char> even unto Yabok <char style="add">[luxuriant emptying river]</char>, and from the wilderness even unto Yarden <char style="add">[Descender]</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="23" style="v" />So now the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> God-Elōhīm <char style="pn">(The Living Word)</char> <char style="add">[The Many Powered]</char> of Yisra’el <char style="add">[He Holds Onto The Heel Of God]</char> has dispossessed the Emori <char style="add">[Highlanders]</char> from before his people Yisra’el <char style="add">[He Holds Onto The Heel Of God]</char>, and should you<char style="ord">i</char> possess it?</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="24" style="v" />Will not you<char style="ord">i</char> possess that which K’mosh <char style="add">[Subduer]</char> your<char style="ord">i</char> god gives you<char style="ord">i</char> to possess? So whomsoever the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> our God-Elōhīm <char style="pn">(The Living Word)</char> <char style="add">[The Many Powered]</char> shall drive out from before us, them will we possess.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="25" style="v" />And now <char style="add">[are]</char> you<char style="ord">i</char> anything better than Balak <char style="add">[Devastator]</char> the son of Zippor <char style="add">[Sparrow]</char>, king of Mo’av <char style="add">[Seed of my Father]</char>? did he ever strive against Yisra’el <char style="add">[He Holds Onto The Heel Of God]</char>, or did he ever fight against them,</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="26" style="v" />While Yisra’el <char style="add">[He Holds Onto The Heel Of God]</char> dwelt in Heshbon <char style="add">[Stronghold]</char> and her towns, and in ‘Aeo’er <char style="add">[Ruins]</char> and her towns, and in all the cities that <char style="add">[be]</char> along by the coasts of ‘Arnon <char style="add">[Rushing Stream]</char>, three hundred years? why therefore did you<char style="ord">2f</char> not recover <char style="add">[them]</char> within that time?</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="27" style="v" />For what reason I have not sinned against you<char style="ord">i</char>, but you<char style="ord">i</char> do me wrong to war against me: let Yehovah HaShofet <char style="add">[Messiah Pre-Incarnate The Judge]</char> be judge this day between the people of Yisra’el <char style="add">[He Holds Onto The Heel Of God]</char> and the children of ‘Amon <char style="add">[Inbred]</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="28" style="v" />However the king of the children of ‘Amon <char style="add">[Inbred]</char> listened not unto the words of Yiftach <char style="add">[He Opens]</char> which he sent him.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="29" style="v" />Then the Spirit of the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> came upon Yiftach <char style="add">[He Opens]</char>, and he passed over Gil’ad <char style="add">[Rocky Region]</char>, and M’nasheh <char style="add">[Causing to Forget]</char>, and passed over Mitzpah <char style="add">[Watchtower]</char> of Gil’ad <char style="add">[Rocky Region]</char>, and from Mitzpah <char style="add">[Watchtower]</char> of Gil’ad <char style="add">[Rocky Region]</char> he passed over <char style="add">[unto]</char> the children of ‘Amon <char style="add">[Inbred]</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="30" style="v" />And Yiftach <char style="add">[He Opens]</char> vowed a vow unto the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char>, and said, If you<char style="ord">i</char> shall without fail deliver the children of ‘Amon <char style="add">[Inbred]</char> into my hands,</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="31" style="v" />Then it shall be, that whatsoever comes forth of the doors of my house to meet me, when I return in peace from the children of ‘Amon <char style="add">[Inbred]</char>, shall surely be the LORD-Yehōvah’s <char style="add">[Messiah Pre-Incarnate]</char>, and I will offer it up for a burnt offering.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="32" style="v" />So Yiftach <char style="add">[He Opens]</char> passed over unto the children of ‘Amon <char style="add">[Inbred]</char> to fight against them; and the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> delivered them into his hands.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="33" style="v" />And he struck them from ‘Aeo’er <char style="add">[Ruins]</char>, even till you<char style="ord">i</char> come to Minnit <char style="add">[distribution]</char>, <char style="add">[even]</char> twenty cities, and unto the plain of the vineyards, with a very great slaughter. Thus the children of ‘Amon <char style="add">[Inbred]</char> were subdued before the people of Yisra’el <char style="add">[He Holds Onto The Heel Of God]</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="34" style="v" />And Yiftach <char style="add">[He Opens]</char> came to Mitzpah <char style="add">[Watchtower]</char> unto his house, and, behold, his daughter came out to meet him with timbrels and with dances: and she <char style="add">[was his]</char> only child; beside her he had neither son nor daughter.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="35" style="v" />And it came to pass, when he saw her, that he rent his clothes, and said, Alas, my daughter! you<char style="ord">i</char> have brought me very low, and you<char style="ord">i</char> are one of them that trouble me: for I have opened my mouth unto the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char>, and I cannot go back.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="36" style="v" />And she said unto him, My father, <char style="add">[if]</char> you<char style="ord">i</char> have opened you<char style="ord">i</char> mouth unto the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char>, do to me according to that which has proceeded out of you<char style="ord">i</char> mouth; forasmuch as the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> has taken vengeance for you<char style="ord">i</char> of you<char style="ord">i</char> enemies, <char style="add">[even]</char> of the children of ‘Amon <char style="add">[Inbred]</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="37" style="v" />And she said unto her father, Let this thing be done for me: let me alone two months, that I may go up and down upon the mountains, and bewail my virginity, I and my fellows.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="38" style="v" />And he said, Go. And he sent her away <char style="add">[for]</char> two months: and she went with her companions, and bewailed her virginity upon the mountains.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="39" style="v" />And it came to pass at the end of two months, that she returned unto her father, who did with her <char style="add">[according]</char> to his vow which he had vowed: and she knew no man. And it was a custom in Yisra’el <char style="add">[He Holds Onto The Heel Of God]</char>,</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="40" style="v" />
    <char style="add">[That]</char> the daughters of Yisra’el <char style="add">[He Holds Onto The Heel Of God]</char> went yearly to lament the daughter of Yiftach <char style="add">[He Opens]</char> the Gil’adi <char style="add">[Hill of Testimony]</char> four days in a year.</para>
  <chapter number="12" style="c" />
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="1" style="v" />And the men of Efrayim <char style="add">[Doubly Fruitful]</char> gathered themselves together, and went northward, and said unto Yiftach <char style="add">[He Opens]</char>, For what reason passed you<char style="ord">i</char> over to fight against the children of ‘Amon <char style="add">[Inbred]</char>, and did not call us to go with you<char style="ord">i</char>? we will burn your<char style="ord">i</char> house upon you<char style="ord">i</char> with fire.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="2" style="v" />And Yiftach <char style="add">[He Opens]</char> said unto them, I and my people were at great strife with the children of ‘Amon <char style="add">[Inbred]</char>; and when I called you, you<char style="ord">2f</char> delivered me not out of their hands.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="3" style="v" />And when I saw that you<char style="ord">2f</char> delivered <char style="add">[me]</char> not, I put my life in my hands, and passed over against the children of ‘Amon <char style="add">[Inbred]</char>, and the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> delivered them into my hand: wherefore then are you<char style="ord">2f</char> come up unto me this day, to fight against me?</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="4" style="v" />Then Yiftach <char style="add">[He Opens]</char> gathered together all the men of Gil’ad <char style="add">[Rocky Region]</char>, and fought with Efrayim <char style="add">[Doubly Fruitful]</char>: and the men of Gil’ad <char style="add">[Rocky Region]</char> struck Efrayim <char style="add">[Doubly Fruitful]</char>, because they said, You<char style="ord">2f</char> Gil’adi <char style="add">[are]</char> fugitives of Efrayim <char style="add">[Doubly Fruitful]</char> among the Efrayim <char style="add">[Doubly Fruitful]</char>, <char style="add">[and]</char> among the M’nasheh <char style="add">[Causing to Forget]</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="5" style="v" />And the Gil’adi took the passages of Yarden <char style="add">[Descender]</char> before the Efrayim <char style="add">[Doubly Fruitful]</char>: and it was <char style="add">[so]</char>, that when those Efrayim <char style="add">[Doubly Fruitful]</char> which were escaped said, Let me go over; that the men of Gil’ad <char style="add">[Rocky Region]</char> aid unto him, <char style="add">[Are]</char> you<char style="ord">i</char> an Efrayimiti <char style="add">[Doubly Fruitful]</char>? If he said, No;</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="6" style="v" />Then said they unto him, Say now Shibbolet <char style="add">[Flowing Stream]</char>: and he said Sibbolet <char style="add">[Ear of Grain or Wheat]</char>: for he could not frame to pronounce <char style="add">[it]</char> right. Then they took him, and killed him at the passages of Yarden <char style="add">[Descender]</char>: and there fell at that time of the Efrayim <char style="add">[Doubly Fruitful]</char> forty and two thousand.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="7" style="v" />And Yiftach <char style="add">[He Opens]</char> judged Yisra’el <char style="add">[He Holds Onto The Heel Of God]</char> six years. Then died Yiftach <char style="add">[He Opens]</char> the Gil’adi <char style="add">[Hill of Testimony]</char>, and was buried in <char style="add">[one of]</char> the cities of Gil’ad <char style="add">[Rocky Region]</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="8" style="v" />And after him Ibtzan <char style="add">[Their Whiteness]</char> of Beit-Lechem <char style="add">[House of Bread]</char> judged Yisra’el <char style="add">[He Holds Onto The Heel Of God]</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="9" style="v" />And he had thirty sons, and thirty daughters, <char style="add">[whom]</char> he sent abroad, and took in thirty daughters from abroad for his sons. And he judged Yisra’el <char style="add">[He Holds Onto The Heel Of God]</char> seven years.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="10" style="v" />Then died Ibtzan <char style="add">[Their Whiteness]</char>, and was buried at Beit-Lechem <char style="add">[House of Bread]</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="11" style="v" />And after him Elon <char style="add">[Mighty]</char>, a Z’vuluni <char style="add">[Wished-For Habitation]</char>, judged Yisra’el <char style="add">[He Holds Onto The Heel Of God]</char>; and he judged Yisra’el <char style="add">[He Holds Onto The Heel Of God]</char> ten years.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="12" style="v" />And Elon <char style="add">[Mighty]</char> the Z’vuluni <char style="add">[Wished-For Habitation]</char> died, and was buried in Ayalon <char style="add">[Field of Deer]</char> in the country of Z’vulun <char style="add">[Glorious Dwelling Place]</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="13" style="v" />And after him Avdon <char style="add">[Servile]</char> the son of Hillel <char style="add">[Praising]</char>, a Pir’atoni <char style="add">[Princely]</char>, judged Yisra’el <char style="add">[He Holds Onto The Heel Of God]</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="14" style="v" />And he had forty sons and thirty nephews, that rode on threescore and ten ass colts: and he judged Yisra’el <char style="add">[He Holds Onto The Heel Of God]</char> eight years.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="15" style="v" />And Avdon <char style="add">[Servile]</char> the son of Hillel <char style="add">[Praising]</char> the Pir’atoni <char style="add">[Princely]</char> died, and was buried in Pir’aton <char style="add">[Princely]</char> in the land of Efrayim <char style="add">[Doubly Fruitful]</char>, in the mount of the ‘Amalekim <char style="add">[Dwellers in a Valley]</char>.</para>
  <chapter number="13" style="c" />
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="1" style="v" />And the people of Yisra’el <char style="add">[He Holds Onto The Heel Of God]</char> did evil again in the sight of the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char>; and the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> delivered them into the hand of the P’lishtim <char style="add">[Immigrants]</char> forty years.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="2" style="v" />And there was a certain man of Tzor’ah <char style="add">[Hornet]</char>, of the family of the Dani <char style="pn">(Dan)</char> <char style="add">[Judge]</char>, whose name <char style="add">[was]</char> Manoach <char style="add">[Rest]</char>; and his wife <char style="add">[was]</char> barren, and bore not.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="3" style="v" />And the angel of the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> appeared unto the woman, and said unto her, Behold now, you<char style="ord">i</char> <char style="add">[are]</char> barren, and bear not: but you<char style="ord">i</char> shall conceive, and bear a son.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="4" style="v" />Now therefore beware, I pray you<char style="ord">i</char>, and drink not wine nor strong drink, and eat not any unclean <char style="add">[thing]</char>:</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="5" style="v" />For, lo, you<char style="ord">i</char> shall conceive, and bear a son; and no razor shall come on his head: for the child shall be a Nazir <char style="add">[One Separated]</char> unto God-Elōhīm <char style="pn">(The Living Word)</char> <char style="add">[The Many Powered]</char> from the womb: and he shall begin to deliver Yisra’el <char style="add">[He Holds Onto The Heel Of God]</char> out of the hand of the P’lishtim <char style="add">[Immigrants]</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="6" style="v" />Then the woman came and told her husband, saying, A man of God-Elōhīm <char style="pn">(The Living Word)</char> <char style="add">[The Many Powered]</char> came unto me, and his Countenance <char style="pn">(Face, appearance; show favor)</char> <char style="add">[was]</char> like the Countenance <char style="pn">(Face, appearance; show favor)</char> of an angel of God-Elōhīm <char style="pn">(The Living Word)</char> <char style="add">[The Many Powered]</char>, very terrible: but I asked him not from what place he <char style="add">[was]</char>, neither told he me his name:</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="7" style="v" />But he said unto me, Behold, you<char style="ord">i</char> shall conceive, and bear a son; and now drink no wine nor strong drink, neither eat any unclean <char style="add">[thing]</char>: for the child shall be a Nazir <char style="add">[One Separated]</char> to God-Elōhīm <char style="pn">(The Living Word)</char> <char style="add">[The Many Powered]</char> from the womb to the day of his death.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="8" style="v" />Then Manoach <char style="add">[Rest]</char> entreated the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char>, and said, O my Lord, let the man of God-Elōhīm <char style="pn">(The Living Word)</char> <char style="add">[The Many Powered]</char> which you<char style="ord">i</char> did send come again unto us, and teach us what we shall do unto the child that shall be born.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="9" style="v" />And God-Elōhīm <char style="pn">(The Living Word)</char> <char style="add">[The Many Powered]</char> listened to the voice of Manoach <char style="add">[Rest]</char>; and the angel of God-Elōhīm <char style="pn">(The Living Word)</char> <char style="add">[The Many Powered]</char> came again unto the woman as she sat in the field: but Manoach <char style="add">[Rest]</char> her husband <char style="add">[was]</char> not with her.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="10" style="v" />And the woman made haste, and ran, and showed her husband, and said unto him, Behold, the man has appeared unto me, that came unto me the <char style="add">[other]</char> day.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="11" style="v" />And Manoach <char style="add">[Rest]</char> arose, and went after his wife, and came to the man, and said unto him, <char style="add">[Are]</char> you<char style="ord">i</char> the man that spoke unto the woman? And he said, I <char style="add">[am]</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="12" style="v" />And Manoach <char style="add">[Rest]</char> said, Now let you<char style="ord">i</char> words come to pass. How shall we order the child, and <char style="add">[how]</char> shall we do unto him?</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="13" style="v" />And the angel of the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> said unto Manoach <char style="add">[Rest]</char>, Of all that I said unto the woman let her beware.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="14" style="v" />She may not eat of any <char style="add">[thing]</char> that comes of the vine, neither let her drink wine or strong drink, nor eat any unclean <char style="add">[thing]</char>: all that I commanded her let her observe.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="15" style="v" />And Manoach <char style="add">[Rest]</char> said unto the angel of the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char>, I pray you<char style="ord">i</char>, let us detain you<char style="ord">i</char>, until we shall have made ready a kid for you<char style="ord">i</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="16" style="v" />And the angel of the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> said unto Manoach <char style="add">[Rest]</char>, Though you<char style="ord">i</char> detain me, I will not eat of your<char style="ord">i</char> bread: and if you<char style="ord">i</char> will offer a burnt offering, you<char style="ord">i</char> must offer it unto the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char>. For Manoach <char style="add">[Rest]</char> knew not that he <char style="add">[was]</char> an angel of the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="17" style="v" />And Manoach <char style="add">[Rest]</char> said unto the angel of the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char>, What <char style="add">[is]</char> your<char style="ord">i</char> name, that when your<char style="ord">i</char> sayings come to pass we may do you<char style="ord">i</char> honour?</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="18" style="v" />And the angel of the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> said unto him, Why ask you<char style="ord">i</char> thus after my name, seeing it <char style="add">[is]</char> secret?</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="19" style="v" />So Manoach <char style="add">[Rest]</char> took a kid with a meat offering, and offered <char style="add">[it]</char> upon a rock unto the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char>: and <char style="add">[the angel]</char> did wondrously; and Manoach <char style="add">[Rest]</char> and his wife looked on.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="20" style="v" />For it came to pass, when the flame went up toward heaven from off the altar, that the angel of the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> ascended in the flame of the altar. And Manoach <char style="add">[Rest]</char> and his wife looked on <char style="add">[it]</char>, and fell on their faces to the ground.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="21" style="v" />But the angel of the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> did no more appear to Manoach <char style="add">[Rest]</char> and to his wife. Then Manoach <char style="add">[Rest]</char> knew that he <char style="add">[was]</char> an angel of the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="22" style="v" />And Manoach <char style="add">[Rest]</char> said unto his wife, We shall surely die, because we have seen God-Elōhīm <char style="pn">(The Living Word)</char> <char style="add">[The Many Powered]</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="23" style="v" />But his wife said unto him, If the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> were pleased to kill us, he would not have received a burnt offering and a meat offering at our hands, neither would he have showed us all these <char style="add">[things]</char>, nor would as at this time have told us <char style="add">[such things]</char> as these.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="24" style="v" />And the woman bore a son, and called his name Shimshon <char style="add">[Like the Sun]</char>: and the child grew, and the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> Blessed <char style="pn">(Favored by God; happy; prosperous)</char> him.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="25" style="v" />And the Spirit of the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> began to move him at times in the camp of Dan <char style="add">[Judge]</char> between Tzor’ah <char style="add">[Hornet]</char> and Eshta’ol <char style="add">[Entreaty]</char>.</para>
  <chapter number="14" style="c" />
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="1" style="v" />And Shimshon <char style="add">[Like the Sun]</char> went down to Timnah <char style="add">[Portion] [Portion]</char>, and saw a woman in Timnah <char style="add">[Portion] [Portion]</char> of the daughters of the P’lishtim <char style="add">[Immigrants]</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="2" style="v" />And he came up, and told his father and his mother, and said, I have seen a woman in Timnah <char style="add">[Portion] [Portion]</char> of the daughters of the P’lishtim <char style="add">[Immigrants]</char>: now therefore get her for me to wife.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="3" style="v" />Then his father and his mother said unto him, <char style="add">[Is there]</char> never a woman among the daughters of your<char style="ord">i</char> brethren, or among all my people, that you<char style="ord">i</char> go to take a wife of the uncircumcised P’lishtim <char style="add">[Immigrants]</char>? And Shimshon <char style="add">[Like the Sun]</char> said unto his father, Get her for me; for she pleases me well.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="4" style="v" />But his father and his mother knew not that it <char style="add">[was]</char> of the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char>, that he sought an occasion against the P’lishtim <char style="add">[Immigrants]</char>: for at that time the P’lishtim <char style="add">[Immigrants]</char> had dominion over Yisra’el <char style="add">[He Holds Onto The Heel Of God]</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="5" style="v" />Then went Shimshon <char style="add">[Like the Sun]</char> down, and his father and his mother, to Timnah <char style="add">[Portion] [Portion]</char>, and came to the vineyards of Timnah <char style="add">[Portion] [Portion]</char>: and, behold, a young lion roared against him.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="6" style="v" />And the Spirit of the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> came mightily upon him, and he rent him as he would have rent a kid, and <char style="add">[he had]</char> nothing in his hand: but he told not his father or his mother what he had done.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="7" style="v" />And he went down, and talked with the woman; and she pleased Shimshon <char style="add">[Like the Sun]</char> well.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="8" style="v" />And after a time he returned to take her, and he turned aside to see the carcass of the lion: and, behold, <char style="add">[there was]</char> a swarm of bees and honey in the carcass of the lion.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="9" style="v" />And he took thereof in his hands, and went on eating, and came to his father and mother, and he gave them, and they did eat: but he told not them that he had taken the honey out of the carcass of the lion.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="10" style="v" />So his father went down unto the woman: and Shimshon <char style="add">[Like the Sun]</char> made there a feast; for so used the young men to do.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="11" style="v" />And it came to pass, when they saw him, that they brought thirty companions to be with him.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="12" style="v" />And Shimshon <char style="add">[Like the Sun]</char> said unto them, I will now put forth a riddle unto you: if you<char style="ord">2f</char> can certainly declare it me within the seven days of the feast, and find <char style="add">[it]</char> out, then I will give you thirty sheets and thirty change of garments:</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="13" style="v" />But if you<char style="ord">2f</char> cannot declare <char style="add">[it]</char> me, then shall you<char style="ord">2f</char> give me thirty sheets and thirty change of garments. And they said unto him, Put forth you<char style="ord">i</char> riddle, that we may hear it.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="14" style="v" />And he said unto them, Out of the eater came forth meat, and out of the strong came forth sweetness. And they could not in three days expound the riddle.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="15" style="v" />And it came to pass on the seventh day, that they said unto Shimshon <char style="add">[Like the Sun]</char>’s wife, Entice your<char style="ord">i</char> husband, that he may declare unto us the riddle, lest we burn you<char style="ord">i</char> and your<char style="ord">i</char> father’s house with fire: have you<char style="ord">2f</char> called us to take that we have? <char style="add">[is it]</char> not <char style="add">[so]</char>?</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="16" style="v" />And Shimshon’s <char style="add">[Like the Sun]</char>’s wife wept before him, and said, you<char style="ord">i</char> do but hate me, and love me not: you<char style="ord">i</char> have put forth a riddle unto the children of my people, and have not told <char style="add">[it]</char> me. And he said unto her, Behold, I have not told <char style="add">[it]</char> my father nor my mother, and shall I tell <char style="add">[it]</char> you<char style="ord">i</char>?</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="17" style="v" />And she wept before him the seven days, while their feast lasted: and it came to pass on the seventh day, that he told her, because she lay sore upon him: and she told the riddle to the children of her people.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="18" style="v" />And the men of the city said unto him on the seventh day before the sun went down, What <char style="add">[is]</char> sweeter than honey? and what <char style="add">[is]</char> stronger than a lion? And he said unto them, If you<char style="ord">2f</char> had not plowed with my heifer, you<char style="ord">2f</char> had not found out my riddle.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="19" style="v" />And the Spirit of the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> came upon him, and he went down to Ashkelon [The Fire of Infamy: I shall be Weighed], and killed thirty men of them, and took their spoil <char style="pn">(plunder; prey; booty)</char>, and gave change of garments unto them which expounded the riddle. And his anger was kindled, and he went up to his father’s house.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="20" style="v" />But Shimshon’s <char style="add">[Like the Sun]</char>’s wife was <char style="add">[given]</char> to his companion, whom he had used as his friend.</para>
  <chapter number="15" style="c" />
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="1" style="v" />But it came to pass within a while after, in the time of wheat harvest, that Shimshon <char style="add">[Like the Sun]</char> visited his wife with a kid; and he said, I will go in to my wife into the chamber. But her father would not suffer him to go in.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="2" style="v" />And her father said, I truly thought that you<char style="ord">i</char> had utterly hated her; therefore I gave her to your<char style="ord">i</char> companion: <char style="add">[is]</char> not her younger sister fairer than she? take her, I pray you<char style="ord">i</char>, instead of her.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="3" style="v" />And Shimshon <char style="add">[Like the Sun]</char> said concerning them, Now shall I be more blameless than the P’lishtim <char style="add">[Immigrants]</char>, though I do them a displeasure.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="4" style="v" />And Shimshon <char style="add">[Like the Sun]</char> went and caught three hundred foxes, and took firebrands, and turned tail to tail, and put a torch in the midst between two tails.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="5" style="v" />And when he had set the brands on fire, he let <char style="add">[them]</char> go into the standing corn of the P’lishtim <char style="add">[Immigrants]</char>, and burnt up both the shocks, and also the standing corn, with the vineyards <char style="add">[and]</char> olives.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="6" style="v" />Then the P’lishtim <char style="add">[Immigrants]</char> said, Who has done this? And they answered, Shimshon <char style="add">[Like the Sun]</char>, the son in law of the Timni <char style="pn">(from Timnah [Portion])</char>, because he had taken his wife, and given her to his companion. And the P’lishtim <char style="add">[Immigrants]</char> came up, and burnt her and her father with fire.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="7" style="v" />And Shimshon <char style="add">[Like the Sun]</char> said unto them, Though you<char style="ord">2f</char> have done this, yet will I be avenged of you, and after that I will cease.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="8" style="v" />And he struck them hip and thigh with a great slaughter: and he went down and dwelt in the top of the rock ‘Eitam <char style="add">[Lair of Wild Beasts]</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="9" style="v" />Then the P’lishtim <char style="add">[Immigrants]</char> went up, and pitched in Y’hudah <char style="add">[Let Him (God) Be Praised]</char>, and spread themselves in Lech <char style="add">[Jaw]</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="10" style="v" />And the men of Y’hudah <char style="add">[Let Him (God) Be Praised]</char> said, Why are you<char style="ord">2f</char> come up against us? And they answered, To bind Shimshon <char style="add">[Like the Sun]</char> are we come up, to do to him as he has done to us.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="11" style="v" />Then three thousand men of Y’hudah <char style="add">[Let Him (God) Be Praised]</char> went to the top of the rock ‘Eitam <char style="add">[Lair of Wild Beasts]</char>, and said to Shimshon <char style="add">[Like the Sun]</char>, Know you<char style="ord">i</char> not that the P’lishtim <char style="add">[Immigrants] [are]</char> rulers over us? what <char style="add">[is]</char> this <char style="add">[that]</char> you<char style="ord">i</char> have done unto us? And he said unto them, As they did unto me, so have I done unto them.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="12" style="v" />And they said unto him, We are come down to bind you<char style="ord">i</char>, that we may deliver you<char style="ord">i</char> into the hand of the P’lishtim <char style="add">[Immigrants]</char>. And Shimshon <char style="add">[Like the Sun]</char> said unto them, Swear unto me, that you<char style="ord">2f</char> will not fall upon me yourselves.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="13" style="v" />And they spoke unto him, saying, No; but we will bind you<char style="ord">i</char> fast, and deliver you<char style="ord">i</char> into their hand: but surely we will not kill you<char style="ord">i</char>. And they bound him with two new cords, and brought him up from the rock.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="14" style="v" />
    <char style="add">[And]</char> when he came unto Lech <char style="add">[Jaw]</char>, the P’lishtim <char style="add">[Immigrants]</char> shouted against him: and the Spirit of the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> came mightily upon him, and the cords that <char style="add">[were]</char> upon his arms became as flax that was burnt with fire, and his bands loosed from off his hands.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="15" style="v" />And he found a new jawbone of an ass, and put forth his hand, and took it, and killed a thousand men with that.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="16" style="v" />And Shimshon <char style="add">[Like the Sun]</char> said, With the jawbone of an ass, heaps upon heaps, with the jaw of an ass have I slain a thousand men.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="17" style="v" />And it came to pass, when he had made an end of speaking, that he cast away the jawbone out of his hand, and called that place Ramat-Lechi <char style="add">[Jawbone Heights]</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="18" style="v" />And he was sore athirst, and called on the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char>, and said, you<char style="ord">i</char> have given this great deliverance into the hand of you<char style="ord">i</char> servant: and now shall I die for thirst, and fall into the hand of the uncircumcised?</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="19" style="v" />But God-Elōhīm <char style="pn">(The Living Word)</char> <char style="add">[The Many Powered]</char> clave an hollow place that <char style="add">[was]</char> in the jaw, and there came water out of it; and when he had drunk, his spirit came again, and he revived: wherefore he called the name thereof ‘Ein-HaKorei <char style="add">[The Spring of One Calling]</char>, which <char style="add">[is]</char> in Lech <char style="add">[Jaw]</char> unto this day.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="20" style="v" />And he judged Yisra’el <char style="add">[He Holds Onto The Heel Of God]</char> in the days of the P’lishtim <char style="add">[Immigrants]</char> twenty years.</para>
  <chapter number="16" style="c" />
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="1" style="v" />Then went Shimshon <char style="add">[Like the Sun]</char> to ‘Azah <char style="add">[The Strong]</char>, and saw there an prostitute, and went in unto her.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="2" style="v" />
    <char style="add">[And it was told]</char> the inhabitants of ‘Azah <char style="pn">(‘Azah [The Strong])</char>, saying, Shimshon <char style="add">[Like the Sun]</char> is come here. And they compassed <char style="add">[him]</char> in, and laid wait for him all night in the gate of the city, and were quiet all the night, saying, In the morning, when it is day, we shall kill him.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="3" style="v" />And Shimshon <char style="add">[Like the Sun]</char> lay till midnight, and arose at midnight, and took the doors of the gate of the city, and the two posts, and went away with them, bar and all, and put <char style="add">[them]</char> upon his shoulders, and carried them up to the top of an hill that <char style="add">[is]</char> before Hevron <char style="add">[Seat of Association]</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="4" style="v" />And it came to pass afterward, that he loved a woman in the Valley of Sorek <char style="add">[choice vines]</char>, whose name <char style="add">[was]</char> D’lilah <char style="add">[Feeble]</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="5" style="v" />And the lords of the P’lishtim <char style="add">[Immigrants]</char> came up unto her, and said unto her, Entice him, and see wherein his great strength <char style="add">[lies]</char>, and by what <char style="add">[means]</char> we may prevail against him, that we may bind him to afflict him: and we will give you<char style="ord">i</char> everyone of us eleven hundred <char style="add">[pieces]</char> of silver.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="6" style="v" />And D’lilah <char style="add">[Feeble]</char> said to Shimshon <char style="add">[Like the Sun]</char>, Tell me, I pray you<char style="ord">i</char>, wherein you<char style="ord">i</char> great strength <char style="add">[lies]</char>, and which you<char style="ord">i</char> might be bound to afflict you<char style="ord">i</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="7" style="v" />And Shimshon <char style="add">[Like the Sun]</char> said unto her, If they bind me with seven green remainder that were never dried, then shall I be weak, and be as another man.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="8" style="v" />Then the lords of the P’lishtim <char style="add">[Immigrants]</char> brought up to her seven green remainder which had not been dried, and she bound him with them.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="9" style="v" />Now <char style="add">[there were]</char> men lying in wait, abiding with her in the chamber. And she said unto him, The P’lishtim <char style="add">[Immigrants] [be]</char> upon you<char style="ord">i</char>, Shimshon <char style="add">[Like the Sun]</char>. And he broke the remainder, as a thread of tinder is broken when it touches the fire. So his strength was not known.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="10" style="v" />And D’lilah <char style="add">[Feeble]</char> said unto Shimshon <char style="add">[Like the Sun]</char>, Behold, you<char style="ord">i</char> have mocked me, and told me lies: now tell me, I pray you<char style="ord">i</char>, with which you<char style="ord">i</char> might be bound.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="11" style="v" />And he said unto her, If they bind me fast with new ropes that never were occupied, then shall I be weak, and be as another man.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="12" style="v" />D’lilah <char style="add">[Feeble]</char> therefore took new ropes, and bound him with that, and said unto him, The P’lishtim <char style="add">[Immigrants] [be]</char> upon you<char style="ord">i</char>, Shimshon <char style="add">[Like the Sun]</char>. And <char style="add">[there were]</char> liers in wait abiding in the chamber. And he broke them from off his arms like a thread.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="13" style="v" />And D’lilah <char style="add">[Feeble]</char> said unto Shimshon <char style="add">[Like the Sun]</char>, Till this point in time you<char style="ord">i</char> have mocked me, and told me lies: tell me which you<char style="ord">i</char> might be bound. And he said unto her, If you<char style="ord">i</char> weave the seven locks of my head with the web.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="14" style="v" />And she fastened <char style="add">[it]</char> with the pin, and said unto him, The P’lishtim <char style="add">[Immigrants] [be]</char> upon you<char style="ord">i</char>, Shimshon <char style="add">[Like the Sun]</char>. And he awakened out of his sleep, and went away with the pin of the beam, and with the web.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="15" style="v" />And she said unto him, How can you<char style="ord">i</char> say, I love you<char style="ord">i</char>, when your<char style="ord">i</char> heart <char style="add">[is]</char> not with me? you<char style="ord">i</char> have mocked me these three times, and have not told me wherein your<char style="ord">i</char> great strength <char style="add">[lies]</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="16" style="v" />And it came to pass, when she pressed him daily with her words, and urged him, <char style="add">[so]</char> that his soul was vexed unto death;</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="17" style="v" />That he told her all his heart, and said unto her, There has not come a razor upon my head; for I <char style="add">[have been]</char> a Nazir <char style="add">[One Separated]</char> unto God-Elōhīm <char style="pn">(The Living Word)</char> <char style="add">[The Many Powered]</char> from my mother’s womb: if I be shaven, then my strength will go from me, and I shall become weak, and be like any <char style="add">[other]</char> man.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="18" style="v" />And when D’lilah <char style="add">[Feeble]</char> saw that he had told her all his heart, she sent and called for the lords of the P’lishtim <char style="add">[Immigrants]</char>, saying, Come up this once, for he has showed me all his heart. Then the lords of the P’lishtim <char style="add">[Immigrants]</char> came up unto her, and brought money in their hand.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="19" style="v" />And she made him sleep upon her knees; and she called for a man, and she caused him to shave off the seven locks of his head; and she began to afflict him, and his strength went from him.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="20" style="v" />And she said, The P’lishtim <char style="add">[Immigrants] [be]</char> upon you<char style="ord">i</char>, Shimshon <char style="add">[Like the Sun]</char>. And he awoke out of his sleep, and said, I will go out as at other times before, and shake myself. And he did not know not that the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> was departed from him.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="21" style="v" />But the P’lishtim <char style="add">[Immigrants]</char> took him, and put out his eyes, and brought him down to ‘Azah <char style="add">[The Strong]</char>, and bound him with fetters of brass; and he did grind in the prison house.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="22" style="v" />However the hair of his head began to grow again after he was shaven.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="23" style="v" />Then the lords of the P’lishtim <char style="add">[Immigrants]</char> gathered them together for to offer a great sacrifice unto Dagon their god, and to rejoice: for they said, Our god has delivered Shimshon <char style="add">[Like the Sun]</char> our enemy into our hand.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="24" style="v" />And when the people saw him, they praised their god: for they said, Our god has delivered into our hands our enemy, and the destroyer of our country, which killed many of us.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="25" style="v" />And it came to pass, when their hearts were merry, that they said, Call for Shimshon <char style="add">[Like the Sun]</char>, that he may make us sport. And they called for Shimshon <char style="add">[Like the Sun]</char> out of the prison house; and he made them sport: and they set him between the pillars.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="26" style="v" />And Shimshon <char style="add">[Like the Sun]</char> said unto the boy that held him by the hand, Suffer me that I may feel the pillars whereupon the house stands, that I may lean upon them.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="27" style="v" />Now the house was full of men and women; and all the lords of the P’lishtim <char style="add">[Immigrants] [were]</char> there; and <char style="add">[there were]</char> upon the roof about three thousand men and women, that beheld while Shimshon <char style="add">[Like the Sun]</char> made sport.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="28" style="v" />And Shimshon <char style="add">[Like the Sun]</char> called unto the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char>, and said, O Lord-Adonai <char style="add">[Greatest Above All Things]</char> GOD-Yehōvih <char style="pn">(THE FATHER)</char>, remember me, I pray you<char style="ord">i</char>, and strengthen me, I pray you<char style="ord">i</char>, only this once, O God-Elōhīm <char style="pn">(The Living Word)</char> <char style="add">[The Many Powered]</char>, that I may be at once avenged of the P’lishtim <char style="add">[Immigrants]</char> for my two eyes.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="29" style="v" />And Shimshon <char style="add">[Like the Sun]</char> took hold of the two middle pillars upon which the house stood, and on which it was borne up, of the one with his right hand, and of the other with his left.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="30" style="v" />And Shimshon <char style="add">[Like the Sun]</char> said, Let me die with the P’lishtim <char style="add">[Immigrants]</char>. And he bowed himself with <char style="add">[all his]</char> might; and the house fell upon the lords, and upon all the people that <char style="add">[were]</char> in it. So the dead which he killed at his death were more than <char style="add">[they]</char> which he killed in his life.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="31" style="v" />Then his brethren and all the house of his father came down, and took him, and brought <char style="add">[him]</char> up, and buried him between Tzor’ah <char style="add">[Hornet]</char> and Eshta’ol <char style="add">[Entreaty]</char> in the burying place of Manoach <char style="add">[Rest]</char> his father. And he judged Yisra’el <char style="add">[He Holds Onto The Heel Of God]</char> twenty years.</para>
  <chapter number="17" style="c" />
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="1" style="v" />And there was a man of mount Efrayim <char style="add">[Doubly Fruitful]</char>, whose name <char style="add">[was]</char> Mikhay’hu <char style="add">[Who is Like God?]</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="2" style="v" />And he said unto his mother, The eleven hundred <char style="add">[shekels]</char> of silver that were taken from you<char style="ord">i</char>, about which you<char style="ord">i</char> cursed, and spoke of also in my ears, behold, the silver <char style="add">[is]</char> with me; I took it. And his mother said, Blessed <char style="pn">(Favored by God; happy; prosperous)</char> [be you<char style="ord">i</char>] of the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char>, my son.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="3" style="v" />And when he had restored the eleven hundred <char style="add">[shekels]</char> of silver to his mother, his mother said, I had wholly dedicated the silver unto the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> from my hand for my son, to make a graven image and a molten image: now therefore I will restore it unto you<char style="ord">i</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="4" style="v" />Yet he restored the money unto his mother; and his mother took two hundred <char style="add">[shekels]</char> of silver, and gave them to the founder, who made thereof a graven image and a molten image: and they were in the house of Mikhay’hu <char style="add">[Who is Like God?]</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="5" style="v" />And the man Mikhay’hu <char style="add">[Who is Like God?]</char> had an house of gods, and made an ephod <char style="pn">(vest)</char> <char style="pn">(ritual vest)</char>, and teraphim <char style="pn">(household gods)</char> <char style="pn">(household gods)</char>, and consecrated one of his sons, who became his priest.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="6" style="v" />In those days <char style="add">[there was]</char> no king in Yisra’el <char style="add">[He Holds Onto The Heel Of God]</char>, <char style="add">[but]</char> every man did <char style="add">[that which was]</char> right in his own eyes.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="7" style="v" />And there was a young man out of Beit-Lechem <char style="add">[House of Bread]</char> in Y’hudah of the family of Y’hudah <char style="add">[Let Him (God) Be Praised]</char>, who <char style="add">[was]</char> a Levi <char style="pn">(Levite)</char> <char style="add">[Joined to]</char>, and he detained <char style="pn">(held)</char> there.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="8" style="v" />And the man departed out of the city from Beit-Lechem <char style="add">[House of Bread]</char> in Y’hudah to sojourn where he could find <char style="add">[a place]</char>: and he came to mount Efrayim <char style="add">[Doubly Fruitful]</char> to the house of Mikhay’hu <char style="add">[Who is Like God?]</char>, as he journeyed.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="9" style="v" />And Mikhay’hu <char style="add">[Who is Like God?]</char> said unto him, Whence come you<char style="ord">i</char>? And he said unto him, I <char style="add">[am]</char> a Levi <char style="pn">(Levite)</char> <char style="add">[Joined to]</char> of Beit-Lechem <char style="add">[House of Bread]</char> in Y’hudah, and I go to sojourn where I may find <char style="add">[a place]</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="10" style="v" />And Mikhay’hu <char style="add">[Who is Like God?]</char> said unto him, Dwell with me, and be unto me a father and a priest, and I will give you<char style="ord">i</char> ten <char style="add">[shekels]</char> of silver by the year, and a suit of apparel, and you<char style="ord">i</char> victuals <char style="pn">(food for humans)</char>. So the Levi <char style="pn">(Levite)</char> <char style="add">[Joined to]</char> <char style="pn">(Levite)</char> went in.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="11" style="v" />And the Levi <char style="pn">(Levite)</char> <char style="add">[Joined to]</char> was content to dwell with the man; and the young man was unto him as one of his sons.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="12" style="v" />And Mikhay’hu <char style="add">[Who is Like God?]</char> consecrated the Levi <char style="pn">(Levite)</char> <char style="add">[Joined to]</char>; and the young man became his priest, and was in the house of Mikhay’hu <char style="add">[Who is Like God?]</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="13" style="v" />Then said Mikhay’hu <char style="add">[Who is Like God?]</char>, Now know I that the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> will do me good, seeing I have a Levi <char style="pn">(Levite)</char> <char style="add">[Joined to]</char> to <char style="add">[my]</char> priest.</para>
  <chapter number="18" style="c" />
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="1" style="v" />In those days <char style="add">[there was]</char> no king in Yisra’el <char style="add">[He Holds Onto The Heel Of God]</char>: and in those days the tribe of the Dani <char style="pn">(Dan)</char> <char style="add">[Judge]</char> sought them an inheritance to dwell in; for unto that day <char style="add">[all their]</char> inheritance had not fallen unto them among the tribes of Yisra’el <char style="add">[He Holds Onto The Heel Of God]</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="2" style="v" />And the children of Dan <char style="add">[Judge]</char> sent of their family five men from their coasts, men of valour, from Tzor’ah <char style="add">[Hornet]</char>, and from Eshta’ol <char style="add">[Entreaty]</char>, to spy out the land, and to search it; and they said unto them, Go, search the land: who when they came to mount Efrayim <char style="add">[Doubly Fruitful]</char>, to the house of Mikhay’hu <char style="add">[Who is Like God?]</char>, they lodged there.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="3" style="v" />When they <char style="add">[were]</char> by the house of Mikhay’hu <char style="add">[Who is Like God?]</char>, they knew the voice of the young man the Levi <char style="pn">(Levite)</char> <char style="add">[Joined to]</char>: and they turned in there, and said unto him, Who brought you<char style="ord">i</char> here? and what do you make in this <char style="add">[place]</char>? and what have you<char style="ord">i</char> here?</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="4" style="v" />And he said unto them, Thus and thus deals Mikhay’hu <char style="add">[Who is Like God?]</char> with me, and has hired me, and I am his priest.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="5" style="v" />And they said unto him, Ask counsel, we pray you<char style="ord">i</char>, of God-Elōhīm <char style="pn">(The Living Word)</char> <char style="add">[The Many Powered]</char>, that we may know whether our way which we go shall be prosperous.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="6" style="v" />And the priest said unto them, Go in peace: before the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> <char style="add">[is]</char> your way wherein you<char style="ord">2f</char> go.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="7" style="v" />Then the five men departed, and came to Layish <char style="add">[Lion]</char>, and saw the people that <char style="add">[were]</char> in it, how they dwelt careless, after the manner of the people of Tzidon <char style="add">[Hunting]</char>, quiet and secure; and <char style="add">[there was]</char> no magistrate in the land, that might put <char style="add">[them]</char> to shame in <char style="add">[any]</char> thing; and they <char style="add">[were]</char> far from the people of Tzidon <char style="add">[Hunting]</char>, and had no business with <char style="add">[any]</char> man.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="8" style="v" />And they came unto their brethren to Tzor’ah <char style="add">[Hornet]</char> and Eshta’ol <char style="add">[Entreaty]</char>: and their brethren said unto them, What <char style="add">[say]</char> you<char style="ord">2f</char>?</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="9" style="v" />And they said, Arise, that we may go up against them: for we have seen the land, and, behold, it <char style="add">[is]</char> very good: and <char style="add">[are]</char> you<char style="ord">2f</char> still? be not slothful to go, <char style="add">[and]</char> to enter to possess the land.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="10" style="v" />When you<char style="ord">2f</char> go, you<char style="ord">2f</char> shall come unto a people secure, and to a large land: for God-Elōhīm <char style="pn">(The Living Word)</char> <char style="add">[The Many Powered]</char> has given it into your hands; a place where <char style="add">[there is]</char> no lack of anything that <char style="add">[is]</char> in the earth.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="11" style="v" />And there went from there of the family of the Dani <char style="pn">(Dan)</char> <char style="add">[Judge]</char>, out of Tzor’ah <char style="add">[Hornet]</char> and out of Eshta’ol <char style="add">[Entreaty]</char>, six hundred men appointed with weapons of war.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="12" style="v" />And they went up, and pitched in Kiryat-Ye’arim <char style="add">[City of Forests]</char>, in Y’hudah <char style="add">[Let Him (God) Be Praised]</char>: wherefore they called that place Machaneh-Dan <char style="add">[Camp of (the) Judge]</char> unto this day: behold, <char style="add">[it is]</char> behind Kiryat-Ye’arim <char style="add">[City of Forests]</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="13" style="v" />And they passed there unto mount Efrayim <char style="add">[Doubly Fruitful]</char>, and came unto the house of Mikhay’hu <char style="add">[Who is Like God?]</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="14" style="v" />Then answered the five men that went to spy out the country of Layish <char style="add">[Lion]</char>, and said unto their brethren, Do you<char style="ord">2f</char> know that there is in these houses an ephod <char style="pn">(vest)</char>, and teraphim <char style="pn">(household gods)</char>, and a graven image, and a molten image? now therefore consider what you<char style="ord">2f</char> have to do.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="15" style="v" />And they turned toward it, and came to the house of the young man the Levi <char style="pn">(Levite)</char> <char style="add">[Joined to]</char>, <char style="add">[even]</char> unto the house of Mikhay’hu <char style="add">[Who is Like God?]</char>, and saluted him.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="16" style="v" />And the six hundred men appointed with their weapons of war, which <char style="add">[were]</char> of the children of Dan <char style="add">[Judge]</char>, stood by the entering of the gate.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="17" style="v" />And the five men that went to spy out the land went up, <char style="add">[and]</char> came in there, <char style="add">[and]</char> took the graven image, and the ephod <char style="pn">(vest)</char>, and the teraphim <char style="pn">(household gods)</char>, and the molten image: and the priest stood in the entering of the gate with the six hundred men <char style="add">[that were]</char> appointed with weapons of war.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="18" style="v" />And these went into Mikhay’hu <char style="add">[Who is Like God?]</char>’s house, and fetched the carved image, the ephod <char style="pn">(vest)</char>, and the teraphim <char style="pn">(household gods)</char>, and the molten image. Then said the priest unto them, What do you<char style="ord">2f</char>?</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="19" style="v" />And they said unto him, Hold your<char style="ord">i</char> peace, lay your<char style="ord">i</char> hand upon you<char style="ord">i</char> mouth, and go with us, and be to us a father and a priest: <char style="add">[is it]</char> better for you<char style="ord">i</char> to be a priest unto the house of one man, or that you<char style="ord">i</char> be a priest unto a tribe and a family in Yisra’el <char style="add">[He Holds Onto The Heel Of God]</char>?</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="20" style="v" />And the priest’s heart was glad, and he took the ephod <char style="pn">(vest)</char>, and the teraphim <char style="pn">(household gods)</char>, and the graven image, and went in the midst of the people.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="21" style="v" />So they turned and departed, and put the little ones and the cattle and the carriage <char style="pn">(baggage)</char> before them.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="22" style="v" />
    <char style="add">[And]</char> when they were a good way from the house of Mikhay’hu <char style="add">[Who is Like God?]</char>, the men that <char style="add">[were]</char> in the houses near to Mikhay’hu <char style="add">[Who is Like God?]</char>’s house were gathered together, and overtook the children of Dan <char style="add">[Judge]</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="23" style="v" />And they cried unto the children of Dan <char style="add">[Judge]</char>. And they turned their faces, and said unto Mikhay’hu <char style="add">[Who is Like God?]</char>, What ails you<char style="ord">i</char>, that you<char style="ord">i</char> come with such a company?</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="24" style="v" />And he said, You<char style="ord">2f</char> have taken away my gods which I made, and the priest, and you<char style="ord">2f</char> are gone away: and what have I more? and what <char style="add">[is]</char> this <char style="add">[that]</char> you<char style="ord">2f</char> say unto me, What ails you<char style="ord">i</char>?</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="25" style="v" />And the children of Dan <char style="add">[Judge]</char> said unto him, Let not your<char style="ord">i</char> voice be heard among us, lest angry fellows run upon you<char style="ord">i</char>, and you<char style="ord">i</char> lose your<char style="ord">i</char> life, with the lives of your<char style="ord">i</char> household.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="26" style="v" />And the children of Dan <char style="add">[Judge]</char> went their way: and when Mikhay’hu <char style="add">[Who is Like God?]</char> saw that they <char style="add">[were]</char> too strong for him, he turned and went back unto his house.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="27" style="v" />And they took <char style="add">[the things]</char> which Mikhay’hu <char style="add">[Who is Like God?]</char> had made, and the priest which he had, and came unto Layish <char style="add">[Lion]</char>, unto a people <char style="add">[that were]</char> at quiet and secure: and they struck them with the edge of the sword, and burnt the city with fire.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="28" style="v" />And <char style="add">[there was]</char> no deliverer, because it <char style="add">[was]</char> far from Tzidon <char style="add">[Hunting]</char>, and they had no business with <char style="add">[any]</char> man; and it was in the valley that <char style="add">[lies]</char> by Beit-Rechov <char style="add">[House of the Street]</char>. And they built a city, and dwelt in it.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="29" style="v" />And they called the name of the city Dan <char style="add">[Judge]</char>, after the name of Dan <char style="add">[Judge]</char> their father, who was born unto Yisra’el <char style="add">[He Holds Onto The Heel Of God]</char>: howbeit the name of the city <char style="add">[was]</char> Layish <char style="add">[Lion]</char> at the first.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="30" style="v" />And the children of Dan <char style="add">[Judge]</char> set up the graven image: and Y’honatan <char style="add">[Yehovah has Given]</char>, the son of Gershom <char style="add">[Exiled One]</char>, the son of M’nasheh <char style="add">[Causing to Forget]</char>, he and his sons were priests to the tribe of Dan <char style="add">[Judge]</char> until the day of the captivity of the land.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="31" style="v" />And they set them up Mikhay’hu <char style="add">[Who is Like God?]</char>’s graven image, which he made, all the time that the house of God-Elōhīm <char style="pn">(The Living Word)</char> <char style="add">[The Many Powered]</char> was in Shiloh <char style="add">[Place of Rest]</char>.</para>
  <chapter number="19" style="c" />
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="1" style="v" />And it came to pass in those days, when <char style="add">[there was]</char> no king in Yisra’el <char style="add">[He Holds Onto The Heel Of God]</char>, that there was a certain Levi <char style="pn">(Levite)</char> <char style="add">[Joined to]</char> sojourning on the side of mount Efrayim <char style="add">[Doubly Fruitful]</char>, who took to him a concubine out of Beit-Lechem <char style="add">[House of Bread]</char> in Y’hudah.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="2" style="v" />And his concubine played the whore against him, and went away from him unto her father’s house to Beit-Lechem <char style="add">[House of Bread]</char> in Y’hudah, and was there four whole months.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="3" style="v" />And her husband arose, and went after her, to speak friendly unto her, <char style="add">[and]</char> to bring her again, having his servant with him, and a couple of asses: and she brought him into her father’s house: and when the father of the girl saw him, he rejoiced to meet him.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="4" style="v" />And his father in law, the girl’s father, retained him; and he abode with him three days: so they did eat and drink, and lodged there.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="5" style="v" />And it came to pass on the fourth day, when they arose early in the morning, that he rose up to depart: and the girl’s father said unto his son in law, Comfort you<char style="ord">i</char> heart with a morsel of bread, and afterward go your way.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="6" style="v" />And they sat down, and did eat and drink both of them together: for the girl’s father had said unto the man, Be content, I pray you<char style="ord">i</char>, and wait all night, and let you<char style="ord">i</char> heart be merry.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="7" style="v" />And when the man rose up to depart, his father in law urged him: therefore he lodged there again.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="8" style="v" />And he arose early in the morning on the fifth day to depart: and the girl’s father said, Comfort your<char style="ord">i</char> heart, I pray you<char style="ord">i</char>. And they tarried until afternoon, and they did eat both of them.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="9" style="v" />And when the man rose up to depart, he, and his concubine, and his servant, his father in law, the girl’s father, said unto him, Behold, now the day draws toward evening, I pray you wait all night: behold, the day grows to an end, lodge here, that you<char style="ord">i</char> heart may be merry; and tomorrow get you early on your way, that you<char style="ord">i</char> may go home.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="10" style="v" />But the man would not wait that night, but he rose up and departed, and came over against Y’vus <char style="add">[Threshing Place]</char>, which <char style="add">[is]</char> Yerushalayim <char style="add">[Foundation of Peace]</char>; and <char style="add">[there were]</char> with him two asses saddled, his concubine also <char style="add">[was]</char> with him.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="11" style="v" />
    <char style="add">[And]</char> when they <char style="add">[were]</char> by Y’vus <char style="add">[Threshing Place]</char>, the day was far spent; and the servant said unto his master, Come, I pray you<char style="ord">i</char>, and let us turn in into this city of the Y’vusi <char style="add">[Threshers, Trampled Under Foot]</char>, and lodge in it.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="12" style="v" />And his master said unto him, We will not turn aside here into the city of a stranger, that <char style="add">[is]</char> not of the people of Yisra’el <char style="add">[He Holds Onto The Heel Of God]</char>; we will pass over to Giv’ah <char style="add">[Hill]</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="13" style="v" />And he said unto his servant, Come, and let us draw near to one of these places to lodge all night, in Giv’ah <char style="add">[Hill]</char>, or in Ramah <char style="add">[Hill]</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="14" style="v" />And they passed on and went their way; and the sun went down upon them <char style="add">[when they were]</char> by Giv’ah <char style="add">[Hill]</char>, which <char style="add">[belongs]</char> to Binyamin <char style="add">[Son of the Right Hand/Strength]</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="15" style="v" />And they turned aside there, to go in <char style="add">[and]</char> to lodge in Giv’ah <char style="add">[Hill]</char>: and when he went in, he sat him down in a street of the city: for <char style="add">[there was]</char> no man that took them into his house to lodging.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="16" style="v" />And, behold, there came an old man from his work out of the field at even, which <char style="add">[was]</char> also of mount Efrayim <char style="add">[Doubly Fruitful]</char>; and he detained <char style="pn">(held)</char> in Giv’ah <char style="add">[Hill]</char>: but the men of the place <char style="add">[were of]</char> Benyamin.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="17" style="v" />And when he had lifted up his eyes, he saw a wayfaring man in the street of the city: and the old man said, Where go you<char style="ord">i</char>? and from what place come you<char style="ord">i</char>?</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="18" style="v" />And he said unto him, We <char style="add">[are]</char> passing from Beit-Lechem <char style="add">[House of Bread]</char> in Y’hudah toward the side of mount Efrayim <char style="add">[Doubly Fruitful]</char>; from there <char style="add">[am]</char> I: and I went to Beit-Lechem <char style="add">[House of Bread]</char> in Y’hudah, but I <char style="add">[am now]</char> going to the house of the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char>; and there <char style="add">[is]</char> no man that receives me to house.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="19" style="v" />Yet there is both straw and provender <char style="pn">(food for livestock or cattle)</char> for our asses; and there is bread and wine also for me, and for your<char style="ord">i</char> female servant, and for the young man <char style="add">[which is]</char> with your<char style="ord">i</char> servants: <char style="add">[there is]</char> no lack of anything.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="20" style="v" />And the old man said, Peace <char style="add">[be]</char> with you<char style="ord">i</char>; howsoever <char style="add">[let]</char> all your<char style="ord">i</char> wants <char style="add">[lie]</char> upon me; only lodge not in the street.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="21" style="v" />So he brought him into his house, and gave provender <char style="pn">(food for livestock or cattle)</char> unto the asses: and they washed their feet, and did eat and drink.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="22" style="v" />
    <char style="add">[Now]</char> as they were making their hearts merry, behold, the men of the city, certain sons of Belial <char style="add">[Worthless, Good for Nothing]</char>, beset the house round about, <char style="add">[and]</char> beat at the door, and spoke to the master of the house, the old man, saying, Bring forth the man that came into you<char style="ord">i</char> house, that we may know him.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="23" style="v" />And the man, the master of the house, went out unto them, and said unto them, No, my brethren, <char style="add">[No]</char>, I pray you, do not <char style="add">[so]</char> wickedly; seeing that this man is come into my house, do not this folly.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="24" style="v" />Behold, <char style="add">[here is]</char> my daughter a virgin, and his concubine; them I will bring out now, and you<char style="ord">2f</char> mistreat them, and do with them what seems good unto you: but unto this man do not so vile <char style="pn">(degrading)</char> a thing.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="25" style="v" />But the men would not hearken to him: so the man took his concubine, and brought her forth unto them; and they raped her, and abused her all the night until the morning: and when the day began to spring, they let her go.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="26" style="v" />Then came the woman in the dawning of the day, and fell down at the door of the man’s house where her lord <char style="add">[was]</char>, till it was light.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="27" style="v" />And her lord rose up in the morning, and opened the doors of the house, and went out to go his way: and, behold, the woman his concubine was fallen down <char style="add">[at]</char> the door of the house, and her hands <char style="add">[were]</char> upon the threshold.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="28" style="v" />And he said unto her, Up, and let us be going. But there was no answer. Then the man took her <char style="add">[up]</char> upon an ass, and the man rose up, and got him unto his place.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="29" style="v" />And when he was come into his house, he took a knife, and laid hold on his concubine, and divided <char style="pn">(cut)</char> her, <char style="add">[together]</char> with her bones, into twelve pieces, and sent her into all the coasts of Yisra’el <char style="add">[He Holds Onto The Heel Of God]</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="30" style="v" />And it was so, that all that saw it said, There was no such deed done nor seen from the day that the people of Yisra’el <char style="add">[He Holds Onto The Heel Of God]</char> came up out of the land of Mitzrayim <char style="add">[Egypt - The Narrow Place]</char> unto this day: consider of it, take advice, and speak <char style="add">[your minds]</char>.</para>
  <chapter number="20" style="c" />
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="1" style="v" />Then all the people of Yisra’el <char style="add">[He Holds Onto The Heel Of God]</char> went out, and the congregation was gathered together as one man, from Dan <char style="add">[Judge]</char> even to Be’er-sheva <char style="add">[Well of the sevenfold Oath]</char>, with the land of Gil’ad <char style="add">[Rocky Region]</char>, unto the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> in Mitzpah <char style="add">[Watchtower]</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="2" style="v" />And the chief of all the people, <char style="add">[even]</char> of all the tribes of Yisra’el <char style="add">[He Holds Onto The Heel Of God]</char>, presented themselves in the assembly of the people of God-Elōhīm <char style="pn">(The Living Word)</char> <char style="add">[The Many Powered]</char>, four hundred thousand footmen that drew sword.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="3" style="v" />(Now the children of Binyamin <char style="add">[Son of the Right Hand/Strength]</char> heard that the people of Yisra’el <char style="add">[He Holds Onto The Heel Of God]</char> were gone up to Mitzpah <char style="add">[Watchtower]</char>.) Then said the people of Yisra’el <char style="add">[He Holds Onto The Heel Of God]</char>, Tell <char style="add">[us]</char>, how was this wickedness <char style="add">[committed]</char>?</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="4" style="v" />And the Levi <char style="pn">(Levite)</char> <char style="add">[Joined to]</char>, the husband of the woman that was slain, answered and said, I came into Giv’ah <char style="add">[Hill]</char> that <char style="add">[belongs]</char> to Binyamin <char style="add">[Son of the Right Hand/Strength]</char>, I and my concubine, to lodge.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="5" style="v" />And the men of Giv’ah <char style="add">[Hill]</char> rose against me, and beset the house round about upon me by night, <char style="add">[and]</char> thought to have slain me: and my concubine have they raped, that she is dead.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="6" style="v" />And I took my concubine, and cut her in pieces, and sent her throughout all the country of the inheritance of Yisra’el <char style="add">[He Holds Onto The Heel Of God]</char>: for they have committed shockingly obscene and degrading crime in Yisra’el <char style="add">[He Holds Onto The Heel Of God]</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="7" style="v" />Behold, you<char style="ord">2f</char> <char style="add">[are]</char> all people of Yisra’el <char style="add">[He Holds Onto The Heel Of God]</char>; give here your advice and counsel.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="8" style="v" />And all the people arose as one man, saying, We will not any <char style="add">[of us]</char> go to his tent, neither will we any <char style="add">[of us]</char> turn into his house.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="9" style="v" />But now this <char style="add">[shall be]</char> the thing which we will do to Giv’ah <char style="add">[Hill]</char>; <char style="add">[we will go up]</char> by lot against it;</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="10" style="v" />And we will take ten men of an hundred throughout all the tribes of Yisra’el <char style="add">[He Holds Onto The Heel Of God]</char>, and an hundred of a thousand, and a thousand out of ten thousand, to fetch victual for the people, that they may do, when they come to Giv’ah <char style="add">[Hill]</char> of Binyamin <char style="add">[Son of the Right Hand/Strength]</char>, according to all the folly that they have wrought in Yisra’el <char style="add">[He Holds Onto The Heel Of God]</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="11" style="v" />So all the men of Yisra’el <char style="add">[He Holds Onto The Heel Of God]</char> were gathered against the city, knit together as one man.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="12" style="v" />And the tribes of Yisra’el <char style="add">[He Holds Onto The Heel Of God]</char> sent men through all the tribe of Binyamin <char style="add">[Son of the Right Hand/Strength]</char>, saying, What wickedness <char style="add">[is]</char> this that is done among you?</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="13" style="v" />Now therefore deliver <char style="add">[us]</char> the men, the children of Belial <char style="add">[Worthless, Good for Nothing]</char>, which <char style="add">[are]</char> in Giv’ah <char style="add">[Hill]</char>, that we may put them to death, and put away evil from Yisra’el <char style="add">[He Holds Onto The Heel Of God]</char>. But the children of Binyamin <char style="add">[Son of the Right Hand/Strength]</char> would not hearken to the voice of their brethren the people of Yisra’el <char style="add">[He Holds Onto The Heel Of God]</char>:</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="14" style="v" />But the children of Binyamin <char style="add">[Son of the Right Hand/Strength]</char> gathered themselves together out of the cities unto Giv’ah <char style="add">[Hill]</char>, to go out to battle against the people of Yisra’el <char style="add">[He Holds Onto The Heel Of God]</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="15" style="v" />And the children of Binyamin <char style="add">[Son of the Right Hand/Strength]</char> were numbered at that time out of the cities twenty and six thousand men that drew sword, beside the inhabitants of Giv’ah <char style="add">[Hill]</char>, which were numbered seven hundred chosen men.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="16" style="v" />Among all this people <char style="add">[there were]</char> seven hundred chosen men left-handed; everyone could sling stones at an hair <char style="add">[breadth]</char>, and not miss.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="17" style="v" />And the men of Yisra’el <char style="add">[He Holds Onto The Heel Of God]</char>, beside Binyamin <char style="add">[Son of the Right Hand/Strength]</char>, were numbered four hundred thousand men that drew sword: all these <char style="add">[were]</char> men of war.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="18" style="v" />And the people of Yisra’el <char style="add">[He Holds Onto The Heel Of God]</char> arose, and went up to the house of God-Elōhīm <char style="pn">(The Living Word)</char> <char style="add">[The Many Powered]</char>, and asked counsel of God-Elōhīm <char style="pn">(The Living Word)</char> <char style="add">[The Many Powered]</char>, and said, Which of us shall go up first to the battle against the children of Binyamin <char style="add">[Son of the Right Hand/Strength]</char>? And the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> said, Y’hudah <char style="add">[Let Him (God) Be Praised] [shall go up]</char> first.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="19" style="v" />And the people of Yisra’el <char style="add">[He Holds Onto The Heel Of God]</char> rose up in the morning, and encamped against Giv’ah <char style="add">[Hill]</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="20" style="v" />And the men of Yisra’el <char style="add">[He Holds Onto The Heel Of God]</char> went out to battle against Binyamin <char style="add">[Son of the Right Hand/Strength]</char>; and the men of Yisra’el <char style="add">[He Holds Onto The Heel Of God]</char> put themselves in array <char style="pn">(to put on; to clothe)</char> to fight against them at Giv’ah <char style="add">[Hill]</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="21" style="v" />And the children of Binyamin <char style="add">[Son of the Right Hand/Strength]</char> came forth out of Giv’ah <char style="add">[Hill]</char>, and destroyed down to the ground of the Yisra’eli’s that day twenty and two thousand men.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="22" style="v" />And the people the men of Yisra’el <char style="add">[He Holds Onto The Heel Of God]</char> encouraged themselves, and set their battle again in array <char style="pn">(to put on; to clothe)</char> in the place where they put themselves in array <char style="pn">(to put on; to clothe)</char> the first day.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="23" style="v" />(And the people of Yisra’el <char style="add">[He Holds Onto The Heel Of God]</char> went up and wept before the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> until even, and asked counsel of the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char>, saying, Shall I go up again to battle against the children of Binyamin <char style="add">[Son of the Right Hand/Strength]</char> my brother? And the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> said, Go up against him.)</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="24" style="v" />And the people of Yisra’el <char style="add">[He Holds Onto The Heel Of God]</char> came near against the children of Binyamin <char style="add">[Son of the Right Hand/Strength]</char> the second day.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="25" style="v" />And Binyamin <char style="add">[Son of the Right Hand/Strength]</char> went forth against them out of Giv’ah <char style="add">[Hill]</char> the second day, and destroyed down to the ground of the people of Yisra’el <char style="add">[He Holds Onto The Heel Of God]</char> again eighteen thousand men; all these drew the sword.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="26" style="v" />Then all the people of Yisra’el <char style="add">[He Holds Onto The Heel Of God]</char>, and all the people, went up, and came unto the house of God-Elōhīm <char style="pn">(The Living Word)</char> <char style="add">[The Many Powered]</char>, and wept, and sat there before the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char>, and fasted that day until even, and offered burnt offerings and peace offerings before the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="27" style="v" />And the people of Yisra’el <char style="add">[He Holds Onto The Heel Of God]</char> enquired of the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char>, (for the ark of the covenant of God-Elōhīm <char style="pn">(The Living Word)</char> <char style="add">[The Many Powered] [was]</char> there in those days,</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="28" style="v" />And Pinchas <char style="add">[mouth of brass]</char>, the son of El’azar <char style="add">[God has helped]</char>, the son of Aharon <char style="add">[Bright, Very High]</char>, stood before it in those days,) saying, Shall I yet again go out to battle against the children of Binyamin <char style="add">[Son of the Right Hand/Strength]</char> my brother, or shall I cease? And the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> said, Go up; for tomorrow I will deliver them into you<char style="ord">i</char> hand.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="29" style="v" />And Yisra’el <char style="add">[He Holds Onto The Heel Of God]</char> set liers in wait round about Giv’ah <char style="add">[Hill]</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="30" style="v" />And the people of Yisra’el <char style="add">[He Holds Onto The Heel Of God]</char> went up against the children of Binyamin <char style="add">[Son of the Right Hand/Strength]</char> on the third day, and put themselves in array <char style="pn">(to put on; to clothe)</char> against Giv’ah <char style="add">[Hill]</char>, as at other times.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="31" style="v" />And the children of Binyamin <char style="add">[Son of the Right Hand/Strength]</char> went out against the people, <char style="add">[and]</char> were drawn away from the city; and they began to strike of the people, <char style="add">[and]</char> kill, as at other times, in the highways, of which one goes up to the house of God-Elōhīm <char style="pn">(The Living Word)</char> <char style="add">[The Many Powered]</char>, and the other to Giv’ah <char style="add">[Hill]</char> in the field, about thirty men of Yisra’el <char style="add">[He Holds Onto The Heel Of God]</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="32" style="v" />And the children of Binyamin <char style="add">[Son of the Right Hand/Strength]</char> said, They <char style="add">[are]</char> smitten down before us, as at the first. But the people of Yisra’el <char style="add">[He Holds Onto The Heel Of God]</char> said, Let us flee, and draw them from the city unto the highways.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="33" style="v" />And all the men of Yisra’el <char style="add">[He Holds Onto The Heel Of God]</char> rose up out of their place, and put themselves in array <char style="pn">(to put on; to clothe)</char> at Ba’al-Tamar <char style="add">[palm-tree]</char> <char style="pn">(lord of the Palms)</char>: and the liers in wait of Yisra’el <char style="add">[He Holds Onto The Heel Of God]</char> came forth out of their places, <char style="add">[even]</char> out of the meadows of Giv’ah <char style="add">[Hill]</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="34" style="v" />And there came against Giv’ah <char style="add">[Hill]</char> ten thousand chosen men out of all Yisra’el <char style="add">[He Holds Onto The Heel Of God]</char>, and the battle was sore: but they knew not that evil <char style="add">[was]</char> near them.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="35" style="v" />And the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> struck Binyamin <char style="add">[Son of the Right Hand/Strength]</char> before Yisra’el <char style="add">[He Holds Onto The Heel Of God]</char>: and the people of Yisra’el <char style="add">[He Holds Onto The Heel Of God]</char> destroyed of the Binyamini that day twenty and five thousand and an hundred men: all these drew the sword.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="36" style="v" />So the children of Binyamin <char style="add">[Son of the Right Hand/Strength]</char> saw that they were smitten: for the men of Yisra’el <char style="add">[He Holds Onto The Heel Of God]</char> gave place to the Binyamini, because they trusted unto the liers in wait which they had set beside Giv’ah <char style="add">[Hill]</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="37" style="v" />And the liers in wait hasted, and rushed upon Giv’ah <char style="add">[Hill]</char>; and the liers in wait drew <char style="add">[themselves]</char> along, and struck all the city with the edge of the sword.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="38" style="v" />Now there was an appointed sign between the men of Yisra’el <char style="add">[He Holds Onto The Heel Of God]</char> and the liers in wait, that they should make a great flame with smoke rise up out of the city.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="39" style="v" />And when the men of Yisra’el <char style="add">[He Holds Onto The Heel Of God]</char> retired in the battle, Binyamin <char style="add">[Son of the Right Hand/Strength]</char> began to strike <char style="add">[and]</char> kill of the men of Yisra’el <char style="add">[He Holds Onto The Heel Of God]</char> about thirty persons: for they said, Surely they are smitten down before us, as <char style="add">[in]</char> the first battle.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="40" style="v" />But when the flame began to arise up out of the city with a pillar of smoke, the Binyamini looked behind them, and, behold, the flame of the city ascended up to heaven.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="41" style="v" />And when the men of Yisra’el <char style="add">[He Holds Onto The Heel Of God]</char> turned again, the men of Binyamin <char style="add">[Son of the Right Hand/Strength]</char> were amazed: for they saw that evil was come upon them.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="42" style="v" />Therefore they turned <char style="add">[their backs]</char> before the men of Yisra’el <char style="add">[He Holds Onto The Heel Of God]</char> unto the way of the wilderness; but the battle overtook them; and them which <char style="add">[came]</char> out of the cities they destroyed in the midst of them.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="43" style="v" />
    <char style="add">[Thus]</char> they enclosed the Binyamini round about, <char style="add">[and]</char> chased them, <char style="add">[and]</char> trampled them down with ease over against Giv’ah <char style="add">[Hill]</char> toward the sunrising.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="44" style="v" />And there fell of Binyamin <char style="add">[Son of the Right Hand/Strength]</char> eighteen thousand men; all these <char style="add">[were]</char> men of valour.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="45" style="v" />And they turned and fled toward the wilderness unto the rock of Rimmon <char style="add">[Pomegranate]</char>: and they gleaned of them in the highways five thousand men; and pursued hard after them unto Gid’om <char style="add">[a cutting down]</char>, and killed two thousand men of them.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="46" style="v" />So that all which fell that day of Binyamin <char style="add">[Son of the Right Hand/Strength]</char> were twenty and five thousand men that drew the sword; all these <char style="add">[were]</char> men of valour.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="47" style="v" />But six hundred men turned and fled to the wilderness unto the rock Rimmon <char style="add">[Pomegranate]</char>, and abode in the rock Rimmon <char style="add">[Pomegranate]</char> four months.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="48" style="v" />And the men of Yisra’el <char style="add">[He Holds Onto The Heel Of God]</char> turned again upon the children of Binyamin <char style="add">[Son of the Right Hand/Strength]</char>, and struck them with the edge of the sword, as well the men of <char style="add">[every]</char> city, as the beast, and all that came to hand: also they set on fire all the cities that they came to.</para>
  <chapter number="21" style="c" />
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="1" style="v" />Now the men of Yisra’el <char style="add">[He Holds Onto The Heel Of God]</char> had sworn in Mitzpah <char style="add">[Watchtower]</char>, saying, There shall not any of us give his daughter unto Binyamin <char style="add">[Son of the Right Hand/Strength]</char> to wife.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="2" style="v" />And the people came to the house of God-Elōhīm <char style="pn">(The Living Word)</char> <char style="add">[The Many Powered]</char>, and abode there till even before God-Elōhīm <char style="pn">(The Living Word)</char> <char style="add">[The Many Powered]</char>, and lifted up their voices, and wept sore;</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="3" style="v" />And said, O LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> God-Elōhīm <char style="pn">(The Living Word)</char> <char style="add">[The Many Powered]</char> of Yisra’el <char style="add">[He Holds Onto The Heel Of God]</char>, why is this come to pass in Yisra’el <char style="add">[He Holds Onto The Heel Of God]</char>, that there should be to day one tribe lacking in Yisra’el <char style="add">[He Holds Onto The Heel Of God]</char>?</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="4" style="v" />And it came to pass on the morrow, that the people rose early, and built there an altar, and offered burnt offerings and peace offerings.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="5" style="v" />And the people of Yisra’el <char style="add">[He Holds Onto The Heel Of God]</char> said, Who <char style="add">[is there]</char> among all the tribes of Yisra’el <char style="add">[He Holds Onto The Heel Of God]</char> that came not up with the congregation unto the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char>? For they had made a great oath concerning him that came not up to the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> to Mitzpah <char style="add">[Watchtower]</char>, saying, He shall surely be put to death.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="6" style="v" />And the people of Yisra’el <char style="add">[He Holds Onto The Heel Of God]</char> repented them for Binyamin <char style="add">[Son of the Right Hand/Strength]</char> their brother, and said, There is one tribe cut off from Yisra’el <char style="add">[He Holds Onto The Heel Of God]</char> this day.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="7" style="v" />How shall we do for wives for them that remain, seeing we have sworn by the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> that we will not give them of our daughters to wives?</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="8" style="v" />And they said, What one <char style="add">[is there]</char> of the tribes of Yisra’el <char style="add">[He Holds Onto The Heel Of God]</char> that came not up to Mitzpah <char style="add">[Watchtower]</char> to the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char>? And, behold, there came none to the camp from Yavesh-Gil’ad <char style="add">[Dry Hill of Testimony]</char> to the assembly.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="9" style="v" />For the people were numbered, and, behold, <char style="add">[there were]</char> none of the inhabitants of Yavesh-Gil’ad <char style="add">[Dry Hill of Testimony]</char> there.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="10" style="v" />And the congregation sent there twelve thousand men of the most valiant, and commanded them, saying, Go and strike the inhabitants of Yavesh-Gil’ad <char style="add">[Dry Hill of Testimony]</char> with the edge of the sword, with the women and the children.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="11" style="v" />And this <char style="add">[is]</char> the thing that you<char style="ord">2f</char> shall do, You<char style="ord">2f</char> shall utterly destroy every male, and every woman that has lain by man.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="12" style="v" />And they found among the inhabitants of Yavesh-Gil’ad <char style="add">[Dry Hill of Testimony]</char> four hundred young virgins, that had known no man by lying with any male: and they brought them unto the camp to Shiloh <char style="add">[Place of Rest]</char>, which <char style="add">[is]</char> in the land of Kena’an <char style="add">[Merchant]</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="13" style="v" />And the whole congregation sent <char style="add">[some]</char> to speak to the children of Binyamin <char style="add">[Son of the Right Hand/Strength]</char> that <char style="add">[were]</char> in the rock Rimmon <char style="add">[Pomegranate]</char>, and to call peaceably unto them.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="14" style="v" />And Binyamin <char style="add">[Son of the Right Hand/Strength]</char> came again at that time; and they gave them wives which they had saved alive of the women of Yavesh-Gil’ad <char style="add">[Dry Hill of Testimony]</char>: and yet so they sufficed them not.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="15" style="v" />And the people repented them for Binyamin <char style="add">[Son of the Right Hand/Strength]</char>, because that the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> had made a breach <char style="pn">(breaking forth; a break; opening, inlet)</char> in the tribes of Yisra’el <char style="add">[He Holds Onto The Heel Of God]</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="16" style="v" />Then the elders of the congregation said, How shall we do for wives for them that remain, seeing the women are destroyed out of Binyamin <char style="add">[Son of the Right Hand/Strength]</char>?</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="17" style="v" />And they said, <char style="add">[There must be]</char> an inheritance for them that be escaped of Binyamin <char style="add">[Son of the Right Hand/Strength]</char>, that a tribe be not destroyed out of Yisra’el <char style="add">[He Holds Onto The Heel Of God]</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="18" style="v" />However we may not give them wives of our daughters: for the people of Yisra’el <char style="add">[He Holds Onto The Heel Of God]</char> have sworn, saying, Cursed <char style="add">[be]</char> he that gives a wife to Binyamin <char style="add">[Son of the Right Hand/Strength]</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="19" style="v" />Then they said, Behold, <char style="add">[there is]</char> a feast of the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> in Shiloh <char style="add">[Place of Rest]</char> yearly <char style="add">[in a place]</char> which <char style="add">[is]</char> on the north side of Beit-El <char style="add">[House of God]</char>, on the east side of the highway that goes up from Beit-El <char style="add">[House of God]</char> to Sh’khem <char style="add">[Shoulder]</char>, and on the south of Levonah <char style="add">[Frankincense]</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="20" style="v" />Therefore they commanded the children of Binyamin <char style="add">[Son of the Right Hand/Strength]</char>, saying, Go and lie in wait in the vineyards;</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="21" style="v" />And see, and, behold, if the daughters of Shiloh <char style="add">[Place of Rest]</char> come out to dance in dances, then come you<char style="ord">2f</char> out of the vineyards, and catch you every man his wife of the daughters of Shiloh <char style="add">[Place of Rest]</char>, and go to the land of Binyamin <char style="add">[Son of the Right Hand/Strength]</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="22" style="v" />And it shall be, when their fathers or their brethren come unto us to complain, that we will say unto them, Be favourable unto them for our sakes: because we reserved not to each man his wife in the war: for you<char style="ord">2f</char> did not give unto them at this time, <char style="add">[that]</char> you<char style="ord">2f</char> should be guilty.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="23" style="v" />And the children of Binyamin <char style="add">[Son of the Right Hand/Strength]</char> did so, and took <char style="add">[them]</char> wives, according to their number, of them that danced, whom they caught: and they went and returned unto their inheritance, and repaired the cities, and dwelt in them.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="24" style="v" />And the people of Yisra’el <char style="add">[He Holds Onto The Heel Of God]</char> departed there at that time, every man to his tribe and to his family, and they went out from there every man to his inheritance.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="25" style="v" />In those days <char style="add">[there was]</char> no king in Yisra’el <char style="add">[He Holds Onto The Heel Of God]</char>: every man did <char style="add">[that which was]</char> right in his own eyes.</para>
</usx>